<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C1017> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        skos:Concept,
        gutprop:Chemical ;
    rdfs:label "Glucuronidase Inhibitor" ;
    rdfs:comment "Any substance that inhibits glucuronidase, an enzyme involved in the hydrolysis of glucuronic acid from glucuronides. One of the key processes by which the human body eliminates toxic chemicals and hormones is by glucuronidation. When beta-glucuronidase deconjugates these glucuronides, it prolongs the stay of the hormone or toxic chemical in the body. Inhibition of glucuronidase can produce chemoprotective effects. [Definition Source: NCIT]",
        "NCIT Match" ;
    skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/Chemical> ;
    gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/b97e9bf0d9342135> .

