<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C26714> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        skos:Concept,
        <https://w3id.org/brainteaser/ontology/schema/DiseaseDisorderOrFinding> ;
    rdfs:label "Celiac Disease" ;
    rdfs:comment "An autoimmune genetic disorder with an unknown pattern of inheritance that primarily affects the digestive tract. It is caused by intolerance to dietary gluten. Consumption of gluten protein triggers an immune response which damages small intestinal villi and prevents adequate absorption of nutrients. Clinical signs include abdominal cramping, diarrhea or constipation and weight loss. If untreated, the clinical course may progress to malnutrition, anemia, osteoporosis and an increased risk of intestinal malignancies. However, the prognosis is favorable with successful avoidance of gluten in the diet. [Definition Source: NCIT]",
        "NCIT Match" ;
    skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/DiseaseDisorderOrFinding> ;
    gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/1dd0b4f576d99d95> ;
    gutprop:target <https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C0027361>,
        <https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C0237401>,
        <https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D000328> .

<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C26723> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        skos:Concept,
        <https://w3id.org/brainteaser/ontology/schema/DiseaseDisorderOrFinding> ;
    rdfs:label "Colitis" ;
    rdfs:comment "Inflammation of the colon. [Definition Source: NCIT]",
        "NCIT Match" ;
    skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/DiseaseDisorderOrFinding> ;
    gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/386cdab8d783c307> .

<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C26732> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        skos:Concept,
        <https://w3id.org/brainteaser/ontology/schema/DiseaseDisorderOrFinding> ;
    rdfs:label "Coronary Artery Disease" ;
    rdfs:comment "NCIT Match",
        "Narrowing of the coronary arteries due to fatty deposits inside the arterial walls. The diagnostic criteria may include documented history of any of the following: documented coronary artery stenosis greater than or equal to 50% (by cardiac catheterization or other modality of direct imaging of the coronary arteries); previous coronary artery bypass surgery (CABG); previous percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI); previous myocardial infarction. (ACC) [Definition Source: NCIT]" ;
    skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/DiseaseDisorderOrFinding> ;
    gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/2afe5e26e9c8cbec>,
        <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/bbc9d6ea9ff4b84b> ;
    gutprop:target <https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/68010361> .

