<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C44459> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        skos:Concept,
        gutprop:Chemical ;
    rdfs:label "Trichloroethylene" ;
    rdfs:comment "A synthetic, light sensitive, volatile, colorless, liquid that is miscible with many non-polar organic solvents. Trichloroethylene is used mainly as a degreaser for metal parts. Upon combustion, it produces irritants and toxic gases. Occupational exposure to trichloroethylene is associated with excess incidences of liver cancer, kidney cancer and non-Hodgkin lymphoma. It is reasonably anticipated to be a human carcinogen. (NCI05) [Definition Source: NCIT]",
        "NCIT Match" ;
    skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/Chemical> ;
    gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/c876549582fb1542>,
