        skos:Concept,
        gutprop:StatisticalTechnique ;
    rdfs:label "Cluster Method" ;
    rdfs:comment "A set of statistical methods used to group variables or observations into strongly inter-related subgroups. In epidemiology, it may be used to analyze a closely grouped series of events or cases of disease or other health-related phenomenon with well-defined distribution patterns in relation to time or place or both. [Definition Source: UMLS]",
        "UMLS Match" ;
