<https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C0021911> rdfs:comment "An intravenous glucose tolerance test is a medical diagnostic procedure that measures the body's ability to clear glucose from the blood after an intravenous injection of glucose, used to diagnose and monitor diabetes and insulin resistance. [Definition Source: llama3-8b-8192]",
        "UMLS Match" .

<https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C0022108> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        skos:Concept,
        gutprop:Chemical ;
    rdfs:label "Irritants" ;
    rdfs:comment "Irritants are substances or agents that cause inflammation, discomfort, or other adverse reactions in living organisms, often through chemical or physical interactions with biological tissues. [Definition Source: llama3-8b-8192]"^^xsd:string,
        "UMLS Match"^^xsd:string ;
