    rdfs:comment "Neuromelanin is a type of melanin pigment produced by the human brain, particularly in the substantia nigra and locus coeruleus, which plays a role in the development and progression of Parkinson's disease. [Definition Source: llama3-8b-8192]"^^xsd:string,
