<https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C0077172> rdfs:comment "Trimethylamine is a volatile organic compound that is a naturally occurring amine found in small amounts in the body, particularly in the gut microbiome, and is also a common component of fish and other seafood. [Definition Source: llama3-8b-8192]",
        "UMLS Match" .

<https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C0085252> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        skos:Concept,
        gutprop:Chemical ;
    rdfs:label "Synapsins" ;
    rdfs:comment "A family of synaptic vesicle-associated proteins involved in the short-term regulation of NEUROTRANSMITTER release. Synapsin I, the predominant member of this family, links SYNAPTIC VESICLES to ACTIN FILAMENTS in the presynaptic nerve terminal. These interactions are modulated by the reversible PHOSPHORYLATION of synapsin I through various signal transduction pathways. The protein is also a substrate for cAMP- and CALCIUM-CALMODULIN-DEPENDENT PROTEIN KINASES. It is believed that these functional properties are also shared by synapsin II. [Definition Source: UMLS]",
        "UMLS Match" ;
    skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/Chemical> ;
    gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/84ba5f572283fbeb> ;
    gutprop:locatedIn <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C45247> .

