<https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C0205753> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        skos:Concept,
        gutprop:Chemical ;
    rdfs:label "Opioid Peptide" ;
    rdfs:comment "The endogenous peptides with opiate-like activity. The three major classes currently recognized are the ENKEPHALINS, the DYNORPHINS, and the ENDORPHINS. Each of these families derives from different precursors, proenkephalin, prodynorphin, and PRO-OPIOMELANOCORTIN, respectively. There are also at least three classes of OPIOID RECEPTORS, but the peptide families do not map to the receptors in a simple way. [Definition Source: UMLS]",
        "UMLS Match" ;
    skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/Chemical> ;
    gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/a66623daa8ee60a9>,
        <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/cbe4fe5f4ab63b51> .

