    rdfs:label "Tail Suspension" ;
    rdfs:comment "Tail suspension is a behavioral test used to assess the analgesic properties of a substance by measuring the response of an animal to a painful stimulus, typically a suspension of its tail. [Definition Source: llama3-8b-8192]",
