    rdfs:label "Biofilm Formation" ;
    rdfs:comment "Biofilm Formation: The process by which microorganisms adhere to a surface and produce a complex matrix of extracellular polymeric substances, leading to the formation of a structured community that is resistant to environmental changes and antimicrobial agents. [Definition Source: llama3-8b-8192]"^^xsd:string,
