        skos:Concept,
        gutprop:Drug ;
    rdfs:label "Esketamine" ;
    rdfs:comment "A cyclohexanone derivative and S-enantiomer of racemic ketamine, with analgesic, anesthetic and antidepressant activities. Although the mechanism of action is not fully understood, upon administration, esketamine targets, non-competitively binds to, and blocks N-methyl D-aspartate (NMDA) receptors. This reduces pain perception, induces sedation, and produce dissociative anesthesia. [Definition Source: UMLS]",
        "UMLS Match" ;
