    rdfs:label "Bacterial 16S Rrna Gene" ;
    rdfs:comment "The \"bacterial_16s_rrna_gene\" refers to a type of gene that encodes the 16S ribosomal RNA (rRNA) subunit in bacteria, which is a key component of the small subunit of the ribosome and is used as a molecular marker for bacterial identification [Definition Source: llama3-8b-8192]",
