    rdfs:label "Behavorial Testing" ;
    dcterms:creator "Samuel Piron" ;
    rdfs:comment "Behavioral testing refers to the scientific method of observing and measuring the behavior of an organism, often in a controlled environment, to assess its cognitive, emotional, or motor functions. [Definition Source: llama3-8b-8192]" ;
