    rdfs:label "Microbiome Analysis" ;
    dcterms:creator "Samuel Piron" ;
    rdfs:comment "Microbiome_analysis refers to the scientific study and analysis of the microbial communities that inhabit a particular environment or ecosystem, typically involving the use of high-throughput sequencing technologies and bioinformatic tools to characterize and understand the composition, diversity, and function of these microbial populations. [Definition Source: llama3-8b-8192]" ;
    skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/BiomedicalTechnique> ;
