<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/species/Mucus-AssociatedSpecies> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        skos:Concept,
        gutprop:Species ;
    rdfs:label "Mucus-Associated Specy" ;
    dcterms:creator "Samuel Piron" ;
    rdfs:comment "\"Mucus-associated_species\" refers to a species of microorganism that is typically found in or on mucus, a thick, protective fluid produced by mucous membranes in the body. [Definition Source: llama3-8b-8192]" ;
