        <https://w3id.org/brainteaser/ontology/schema/DiseaseDisorderOrFinding> ;
    rdfs:label "Salsolinol-Induced Toxicity" ;
    dcterms:creator "Samuel Piron" ;
    rdfs:comment "Salsolinol-induced toxicity refers to the harmful effects caused by the accumulation of salsolinol, a neurotoxin, in the body, which can lead to various physiological and neurological disorders. [Definition Source: llama3-8b-8192]" ;
    skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/DiseaseDisorderOrFinding> ;
    gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/0269ee294e8caf1d>,
