        skos:Concept,
        gutprop:Chemical,
        gutprop:DietarySupplement ;
    rdfs:label "Lipid" ;
    rdfs:comment "A class of hydrocarbon-containing organic compounds. Lipids are insoluble in water but soluble in nonpolar solvents and play important roles in living organisms: these roles include functioning as energy storage molecules, serving as structural components of cell membranes, and constituting important signaling molecules. Lipids can be subdivided into 2 groups: fatty acids and glycerides. [Definition Source: NCIT]",
        "NCIT Match" ;
