<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/21167931_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_21167931_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Clinical, epidemiological and therapeutic studies indicate that some human depression is associated with proinflammatory cytokines, chronic inflammatory disorders, and inflammation-inducing lifestyle factors." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/21167931> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/21167931_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_21167931_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Moreover depression can be induced by administration of proinflammatory cytokines, including IL-2 or IFN-α." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/21167931> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/25034760_12> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_25034760_12" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In summary, this review surveys associative and experimental data linking autoimmunity, GI activity and schizophrenia, and proposes that understanding of disrupted biological pathways outside of the brain can lend valuable information regarding pathogeneses of complex, polygenic brain disorders." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/25034760> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/25034760_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_25034760_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Exposure to wheat gluten and bovine milk casein also contribute to non-celiac food sensitivities in susceptible individuals." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/25034760> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/25173628_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_25173628_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Obese-type gut microbiota induce neurobehavioral changes in the absence of obesity." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/25173628> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/25173628_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_25173628_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The prevalence of mental illness, particularly depression and dementia, is increased by obesity." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/25173628> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/25173628_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_25173628_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The mice given HFD microbiota had significant and selective disruptions in exploratory, cognitive, and stereotypical behavior compared with mice with control diet microbiota in the absence of significant differences in body weight." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/25173628> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/25173628_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_25173628_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Collectively, these data reinforce the link between gut dysbiosis and neurologic dysfunction and suggest that dietary and/or pharmacologic manipulation of gut microbiota could attenuate the neurologic complications of obesity." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/25173628> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/25869281_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_25869281_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Many factors affect gut microbiota; application of broad range antibiotics disturb microbiota, while probiotic application protects the microbiota." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/25869281> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/25869281_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_25869281_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The levels of the mineralocorticoid and N-methyl-D-aspartate receptors were also elevated in the hippocampus of the ampillicin+NS9 treated group." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/25869281> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/25869281_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_25869281_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "NS9 administration also reduced the anxiety-like behaviour and alleviated the ampicillin-induced impairment in memory retention." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/25869281> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/25869281_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_25869281_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Our results highlight how gut contents regulate the brain, and shed light on the clinical applications of probiotics to treat the side effect of antibiotics and mental disorders." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/25869281> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/25911232_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_25911232_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Understanding microbiota-brain interactions is an exciting area of research which may contribute new insights into individual variations in cognition, personality, mood, sleep, and eating behavior, and how they contribute to a range of neuropsychiatric diseases ranging from affective disorders to autism and schizophrenia." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/25911232> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/25940667_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_25940667_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The dormant blood microbiome in chronic, inflammatory diseases." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/25940667> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/25940667_12> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_25940667_12" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Overall, it seems that many more chronic, non-communicable, inflammatory diseases may have a microbial component than are presently considered, and may be treatable using bactericidal antibiotics or vaccines." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/25940667> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/26190966_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_26190966_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Based on recent findings, from studies conducted on animal models of obesity, it has been proposed that inflammatory processes may participate in both the peripheral and brain disorders associated with the obesity condition including the development of emotional and cognitive alterations." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/26190966> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/26190966_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_26190966_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This is supported by the fact that obesity is characterized by peripheral low-grade inflammation, originating from increased adipose tissue mass and/or dysbiosis (changes in gut microbiota environment), both of which contribute to increased susceptibility to immune-mediated diseases." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/26190966> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/26190966_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_26190966_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "These findings give new insights to the pathophysiological mechanisms contributing to the development of brain disorders in the context of obesity and provide valuable data for introducing new therapeutic strategies for the treatment of neuropsychiatric complications often reported in obese patients." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/26190966> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/26408987_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_26408987_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Chronic stress can cause behavioral, cognitive, biochemical, and gut microbiota aberrations." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/26408987> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/26408987_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_26408987_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "It is hypothesized that administration of probiotics can improve chronic-stress-induced depression." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/26408987> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/26923630_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_26923630_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "However, both models have limitations, as germ-free mice display alterations in blood-brain barrier and brain ultrastructure and antibiotics may act directly on the brain." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/26923630> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/26927355_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_26927355_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "How these colon microbiota contribute to the surge of diabetes and whether this new knowledge can be used to control diabetes and metabolic syndrome are questions for future scientific studies." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/26927355> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/27319972_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_27319972_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "However, studies using germ-free animals, infective models, prebiotics, probiotics, and antibiotics have increased our understanding of the interplay." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/27319972> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/27566465_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_27566465_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Alzheimer's disease (AD) is a most common neurodegenerative disorder, which associates with impaired cognition." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/27566465> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/27566465_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_27566465_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The increased permeability of intestine and blood-brain barrier induced by gut microbiota disturbance will increase the incidence of neurodegeneration disorders." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/27566465> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/27698624_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_27698624_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Development of these alternative strategies is predicated on experimental evidence and diligent research on the biology of stress, fear, anxiety-related behaviors, and the gut-brain connection." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/27698624> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/27763700_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_27763700_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "These data suggest early life diets containing prebiotics and/or LAC promote behavioural stress resistance and uniquely modulate gene expression in corresponding circuits." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/27763700> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/27763700_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_27763700_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "All diets altered gut bacteria, while diets containing GOS and PDX increased Lactobacillus spp." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/27763700> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/27763700_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_27763700_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Diets did not attenuate stress effects on spleen weight, corticosterone and blood glucose; however, all diets differentially attenuated stress-induced learned helplessness." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/27763700> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/27763700_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_27763700_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Notably, in situ hybridization revealed that all diets reduced stress-evoked cfos mRNA in the dorsal raphe nucleus (DRN), a structure important for learned helplessness behaviours." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/27763700> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/27900676_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_27900676_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Altered levels of cytokines related to IL-23/IL-17 axis have been observed in schizophrenia patients in a few studies." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/27900676> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28073356_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28073356_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We put forward the hypothesis that gastrointestinal infections with parasitic worms, such as helminths, induce an imbalance of the gut-brain axis, which, in turn, can detrimentally manifest in brain development." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28073356> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28158162_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28158162_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The potential effects of probiotics supplement on migraine headache were also included." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28158162> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28158162_11> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28158162_11" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "There is limited evidence from clinical studies of the positive effects of probiotics in patients with migraine headache." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28158162> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28158162_12> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28158162_12" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Large-scale randomized, placebo-controlled clinical trials are warranted to evaluate the clinical efficacy and safety of probiotics in patients with migraine headache." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28158162> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28158162_13> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28158162_13" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Similar to migraine headache, disorders of the brain involving depression and anxiety have been demonstrated to be associated with increased gut permeability." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28158162> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28158162_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28158162_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The present investigation included a PubMed search using the following terms: migraine headache, gut microbiota, brain function, and probiotics." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28158162> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28399458_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28399458_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Unfortunately, many studies merely focused on perinatal distress without consideration of lifetime anxiety and depressive disorders." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28399458> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28399458_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28399458_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "However, they suggest promising directions regarding our current knowledge about the relevance of maternal perinatal distress for infant inflammatory diseases (e.g." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28399458> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28442250_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28442250_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Numbers of Lactobacillus group bacteria were elevated in FEP-patients and significantly correlated with severity along different symptom domains." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28442250> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28556833_11> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28556833_11" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Therefore, the blockade of IL-6 receptor in the periphery shows promise as a novel therapeutic approach for depressed patients with higher IL-6 blood levels." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28556833> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28556833_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28556833_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Accumulating evidence suggests that pro-inflammatory cytokines such as interleukin-6 (IL-6) have an important role in the pathogenesis of depression." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28556833> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28572752_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28572752_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "<b>Conclusion</b>: The results suggest that patients with a history of alcohol overconsumption suffer from both small intestinal malabsorption and impaired colonic microbial metabolism." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28572752> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28572752_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28572752_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Thirty-five had a history of alcohol overconsumption, 66 had coeliac disease, and 216 had a functional bowel disorder, while 44 healthy controls were included for comparison." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28572752> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28572752_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28572752_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The alcohol overconsumption group had similar small intestinal phase results as the group of patients with untreated coeliac disease." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28572752> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28629758_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28629758_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Implications of the gut microbiota in vulnerability to the social avoidance effects of chronic social defeat in male mice." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/28629758> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28629758_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28629758_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In the present investigation we examined whether microbial changes in cecum contents were associated with social avoidance behaviors, a feature of depression, and pro-inflammatory variations among socially stressed mice." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28629758> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28629758_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28629758_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Mice that were most susceptible to the behavioral effects of chronic social defeat (reflected by severe social avoidance behaviors) displayed the greatest changes within particular sets of bacteria at the phylum and genus taxonomic ranks." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28629758> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28716445_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28716445_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "While the hypothalamus controls both feeding behavior and the stress response, the integration of the neural control centers and the peripheral gut allows for disruption in the gastrointestinal systems and dysfunctional communication to the brain." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28716445> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28716445_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28716445_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Responses to stress have effects on feeding behavior and mood and the regulation of the stress response by the gut microbiota could contribute to the dysfunction seen in patients with psychiatric illnesses." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28716445> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28816544_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28816544_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Depression, anxiety and other affective disorders are globally widespread and severely debilitating human brain diseases." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28816544> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28843021_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28843021_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "To compare microbiota in carefully preserved nasal wash and stool samples of subjects with idiopathic rapid eye movement sleep behavior disorder, manifest PD, and healthy individuals." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28843021> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28843021_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28843021_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Differentially abundant gut microbes, such as Akkermansia, were observed in PD, but no strong differences in nasal microbiota." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28843021> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28852308_11> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28852308_11" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We also consider the stages of life where the gut microbiota is more susceptible to the effects of environmental stressors, and the possible microbiota-targeted intervention strategies that could improve health status and prevent psychiatric disorders in the near future." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28852308> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28852308_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28852308_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Gut microbiota is currently viewed as a key regulator of a fluent bidirectional dialogue between the gut and the brain (gut-brain axis)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28852308> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28852308_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28852308_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Such research is expected to contribute to the design of strategies to modulate the gut microbiota and its functions with a view to improving mental health, and thus provide opportunities to improve the management of psychiatric diseases." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28852308> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28976454_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28976454_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Literature review articles indicate that several psychiatric disorders are associated with altered gut microbiota, whereas evidence linking functional gastrointestinal disorders and dysbiosis has not been firmly established." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28976454> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28976454_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28976454_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Consistent with the literature linking psychiatric disorders with dysbiosis is that life adversity during childhood and certain temperaments that develop early in life are associated with altered gut microbiota, particularly the Prevotella species." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28976454> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/29022384_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_29022384_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We confirmed the clear difference between microbiota of infants born by Caesarean section compared to vaginally delivered infants and the impact of feeding mode on infant gut microbiota." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/29022384> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/29249803_11> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_29249803_11" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Furthermore, the specific effect of (R)-ketamine on the levels of Mollicutes and Butyricimonas may explain its robust antidepressant action." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/29249803> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/29249803_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_29249803_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "At the class level, both ketamine enantiomers significantly attenuated the increase in the levels of Deltaproteobacteria in the susceptible mice after CSDS." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/29249803> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/29249803_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_29249803_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "At the genus level, both ketamine enantiomers significantly attenuated the decrease in the levels of Butyricimonas in the susceptible mice." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/29249803> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/29352709_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_29352709_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "At the phylum level, we found that the abundance of Proteobacteria in the schizophrenia patients was significantly increased." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/29352709> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/29352709_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_29352709_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The receiver operating characteristic curve analysis demonstrated that 12 significant microbiota biomarkers were capable of being used as diagnostic factors for distinguishing the schizophrenia cohort from those in the control cohort (AUC = 0.837)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/29352709> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/29857583_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_29857583_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In recent years evidence has emerged that neurodegenerative diseases (NDs) are strongly associated with the microbiome composition in the gut." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/29857583> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/29857583_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_29857583_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "A decrease of <i>Faecalibacterium</i> spp., <i>Coprococcus</i> spp., <i>Blautia</i> spp., <i>Prevotella</i> spp." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/29857583> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/29857583_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_29857583_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "However, on a higher taxonomic resolution like genus or species level, a minor overlap was observed between PD and MSA, both alpha synucleinopathies." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/29857583> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/29955222_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_29955222_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This variety helps to restore diversity in the gut bacteria and may potentially prevent or reverse chronic disease, such as colon cancer or type 2 diabetes." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/29955222> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30072879_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30072879_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Effects of Sub-Chronic MPTP Exposure on Behavioral and Cognitive Performance and the Microbiome of Wild-Type and mGlu8 Knockout Female and Male Mice." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/30072879> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30072879_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30072879_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Motor dysfunction is a hallmark of Parkinson's disease (PD); however, non-motor symptoms such as gastrointestinal dysfunction often arise prior to motor symptoms." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30072879> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30072879_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30072879_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Alterations in the gut microbiome have been proposed as the earliest event in PD pathogenesis." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30072879> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30072879_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30072879_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We studied whether these effects are associated with changes in striatal tyrosine hydroxylase (TH) levels and the gut microbiome." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30072879> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30309367_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30309367_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Recent findings have linked the microbiota to gastrointestinal disorders characterized by abdominal pain suggesting the ability of microbes to modulate visceral hypersensitivity and nociception to pain." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30309367> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30309367_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30309367_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We included an updated overview of the potential therapeutic effects of dietary intervention, specifically probiotics and prebiotics, in alleviating hypersensitivity to visceral pain stimuli." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30309367> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30309367_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30309367_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The gut microbiota dramatically impacts normal visceral pain sensation and affects the mechanisms mediating visceral nociception." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30309367> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30317530_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30317530_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Recent developments in genome sequencing technologies, bioinformatics and culturomics have enabled researchers to explore the microbiota and in particular their functions at more detailed level than before." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30317530> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30317530_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30317530_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The accumulated evidences suggest that though a part of the microbiota is conserved, the dynamic members vary along the gastrointestinal tract, from infants to elderly, primitive tribes to modern societies and in different health conditions." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30317530> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30394313_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30394313_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The composition and abundance of candidate MEs were compared between the three groups of children." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30394313> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30459574_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30459574_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Oral Probiotics Ameliorate the Behavioral Deficits Induced by Chronic Mild Stress in Mice via the Gut Microbiota-Inflammation Axis." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/30459574> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30459574_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30459574_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In recent years, a burgeoning body of research has revealed links between depression and the gut microbiota, leading to the therapeutic use of probiotics for stress-related disorders." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30459574> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30459574_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30459574_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Thus, the possible mechanism involved in the antidepressant-like activity of probiotics is correlated with <i>Lactobacillus</i> species via the gut microbiota-inflammation-brain axis." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30459574> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30518033_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30518033_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "After 1 week of adaptation, their initial anxiety level was monitored using the EPM test via an EthoVision XT, a standardized software used for behavorial testing." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30518033> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30518033_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30518033_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Changes were observed in host anxiety levels in correlation to the shift of the gut microbiota." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30518033> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30528936_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30528936_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Role of Actinobacteria and Coriobacteriia in the antidepressant effects of ketamine in an inflammation model of depression." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/30528936> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30528936_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30528936_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Ketamine, an N-methyl-d-aspartic acid receptor (NMDAR) antagonist, elicits rapid-acting and sustained antidepressant effects in treatment-resistant depressed patients." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30528936> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30528936_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30528936_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Here we investigated the role of gut microbiota in the antidepressant effects of ketamine in lipopolysaccharide (LPS)-induced inflammation model of depression." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30528936> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30528936_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30528936_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Importantly, the receiver operating characteristic (ROC) curves demonstrated that the phylum Actinobacteria and the class Coriobacteriia were potential biomarker for the antidepressant effects of ketamine in an inflammation model." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30528936> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30528936_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30528936_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "These findings suggest that antidepressant effects of ketamine might be related to the regulation of abnormal composition of gut microbiota, and that the phylum Actinobacteria and the class Coriobacteriia might be potential biomarkers for ketamine's antidepressant efficacy." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30528936> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30584306_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30584306_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Possible association of Firmicutes in the gut microbiota of patients with major depressive disorder." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/30584306> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30584306_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30584306_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This study found that there is a significant disorder of gut microbiota in the patients with depression, in which the Firmicutes decreased significantly." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30584306> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30584306_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30584306_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In this study, we explore the changes and effects of Firmicutes in the patients with major depressive disorder (MDD)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30584306> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30584306_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30584306_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The study shows that the alpha diversity indices of MDD patients are lower than those of the healthy controls." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30584306> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30659564_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30659564_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "According to the recent studies, there is a link between the composition of gut microbiota and mental disorders in animals (response to depression and chronic stress)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30659564> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30701194_13> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30701194_13" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Through a comprehensive gut metagenomic and metabolome study of children with ASD, alterations in gut metabolite composition were found in children with ASD, and these alterations were linked to changes in gut microbiota composition." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30701194> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30701194_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30701194_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Altered glutamate metabolites were found in the ASD group, along with a decline in 2-keto-glutaramic acid and an abundance of microbiota associated with glutamate metabolism." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30701194> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30707176_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30707176_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Vasovagal syncope (VVS) is common in children and greatly affect both physical and mental health." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30707176> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30707176_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30707176_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The relative abundance of Ruminococcaceae in VVS patients was positively correlated with the frequency of syncope (r = 0.616, P < 0.01)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30707176> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30717162_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30717162_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In this study, we aimed to investigate the effects of hospital stay, including escitalopram administration, on gut microbiota in patients with depressive episodes." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30717162> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30818031_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30818031_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Impact of chemotherapy on the association between fear of cancer recurrence and the gut microbiota in breast cancer survivors." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/30818031> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30818031_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30818031_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Multiple regression analysis with adjustment for possible confounders showed that the relative abundance of the Bacteroides genus (beta = 0.180, p = 0.03) was significantly and directly associated with FCR." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30818031> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30900006_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30900006_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Treatment with broad-spectrum antibiotics for 2 weeks resulted in a host-specific physiological response at the gastrointestinal barrier including a decrease in barrier permeability in BALB/c mice and alterations in the expression of barrier regulating genes in both strains." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30900006> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31053995_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31053995_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In the current study we have shown the downregulation of NAPEs in plasma of PD patients and we thus speculate that these lipids might serve as candidate biomarkers for PD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31053995> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31083360_11> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31083360_11" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Prebiotics only improved certain GI symptoms; however, when combined with an exclusion diet (gluten and casein free) showed a significant reduction in anti-sociability scores." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31083360> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31083360_14> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31083360_14" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "<i>Conclusion</i>: Despite promising preclinical findings, prebiotics and probiotics have demonstrated an overall limited efficacy in the management of GI or behavioral symptoms in children with ASD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31083360> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31083360_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31083360_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "There is some anecdotal evidence that probiotics are able to alleviate GI symptoms as well as improve behavioral issues in children with ASD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31083360> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31148353_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31148353_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Current therapies for Parkinson's disease (PD), including L-3,4-dihydroxyphenylalanine (L-DOPA), and clinical trials investigating dopaminergic cell transplants, have generated mixed results with the eventual induction of dyskinetic side effects." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31148353> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31148353_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31148353_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "These novel data directly implicate a key pathological crosstalk between gut and brain ushering a new avenue of therapeutically targeting the gut microbiome with hUCB-derived stem cells and plasma for PD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31148353> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31179435_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31179435_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Anxiety symptoms are common in mental diseases and a variety of physical disorders, especially in disorders related to stress." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31179435> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31179435_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31179435_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "More and more basic studies have indicated that gut microbiota can regulate brain function through the gut-brain axis, and dysbiosis of intestinal microbiota was related to anxiety." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31179435> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31248424_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31248424_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Altered gut microbiota and inflammatory cytokine responses in patients with Parkinson's disease." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/31248424> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31248424_11> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31248424_11" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Altered microbiota was correlated with plasma concentrations of IFNγ and TNFα." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31248424> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31248424_12> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31248424_12" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "There was a correlation between Bacteroides and plasma level of TNFα (rho = 0.638 [95% CI: 0.102-0.887], P = 0.02); and a correlation between Verrucomicrobia abundance and plasma concentrations of IFNγ (rho = 0.545 [95% CI - 0.043-0.852], P = 0.05)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31248424> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31248424_13> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31248424_13" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The elevated plasma cytokine responses were confirmed in an additional independent 120 patients with PD and 120 controls (TNFα: PD vs. control 8.51 ± 4.63 pg/ml vs. 4.82 ± 2.23 pg/ml, P < 0.01; and IFNγ: PD vs. control: 38.45 ± 7.12 pg/ml vs. 32.79 ± 8.03 pg/ml, P = 0.03)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31248424> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31248424_14> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31248424_14" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This study reveals altered gut microbiota in PD and its correlation with clinical phenotypes and severity in our population." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31248424> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31248424_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31248424_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The abundances of Bacteroides were more increased in patients with non-tremor PD subtype than patients with tremor subtype." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31248424> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31255682_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31255682_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Here, eighty-four patients with schizophrenia and 84 sex- and age-matched healthy controls were enrolled." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31255682> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31255682_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31255682_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Patients with schizophrenia had significantly reduced gut microbiota richnesses compared with those of the healthy controls, and the gut microbiota compositions clearly distinguished the patients with schizophrenia from the healthy controls." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31255682> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31377712_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31377712_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "However, the links between disease-specific variables at diagnosis, resilience and psychological adjustment of patients with MS remain largely unexplored, especially in adolescents and young adults." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31377712> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31377712_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31377712_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Comparative statistics (ie, analysis of variance or unpaired samples t-test, correlation and regression analyses) will be applied to evaluate the relationship among biological, psychological and social factors." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31377712> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31383280_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31383280_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Perinatal mood and anxiety disorders (PMAD) have significant negative impacts on mother and child, yet treatments are limited." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31383280> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31488882_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31488882_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Recently, increasing evidence has suggested the association between gut dysbiosis and Alzheimer's disease (AD) progression, yet the role of gut microbiota in AD pathogenesis remains obscure." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31488882> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31493127_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31493127_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Evolutionarily conserved signals that are involved in the communication between microbiota and the host include neuroactive substances (neurochemicals) such as peptides, amino acids, biogenic amines, short-chain fatty acids, and gaseous substances." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31493127> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31493127_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31493127_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Attempts are made to correct imbalances in the brain-gut-microbiota axis with probiotics including their subgroup called psychobiotics that release neuroactive substances directly influencing the human brain, psyche, and behavior." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31493127> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31498131_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31498131_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Here, differences in methodologies and the presence of possible confounders in the study populations are assessed for their potential to confound the results of gut microbiome studies in PD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31498131> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31498131_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31498131_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Gut microbiome studies in PD exhibited considerable variability with respect to the study population, sample transport conditions, laboratory protocols and sequencing, bioinformatics pipelines, and biostatistical methods." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31498131> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31530799_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31530799_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Members of the order Lactobacillales were present at significantly higher levels in the susceptible rats than in control and resilient rats." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31530799> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31530799_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31530799_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "At the family level, the number of Lactobacillaceae in the susceptible rats was significantly higher than in control and resilient rats." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31530799> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31539679_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31539679_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Antibiotic-induced microbiome depletion is associated with resilience in mice after chronic social defeat stress." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/31539679> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31539679_12> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31539679_12" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "These findings suggest that antibiotic-induced microbiome depletion contributed to resilience to anhedonia in mice subjected to CSDS." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31539679> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31596658_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31596658_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "<b><i>Conclusions</i>:</b> In consideration of the known effects of PBM on metabolomics, and the now demonstrated effects of PBM on the microbiome, as well as other effects of light on the microbiome, including modulating circadian rhythms, the present perspective introduces a new term \"photobiomics\" and looks forward to the application of PBM to influence the microbiome in humans." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31596658> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31610228_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31610228_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Plasma cytokine levels in patients with chronic alcohol overconsumption: Relations to gut microbiota markers and clinical correlates." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/31610228> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31610228_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31610228_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Patients with alcohol overconsumption reported more psychiatric symptoms, and these symptoms were inversely correlated with IL-10 levels." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31610228> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31610228_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31610228_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We included hospital inpatients with a history of chronic alcohol overconsumption." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31610228> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31610228_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31610228_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We then examined associations of cytokine levels with the abundance of Proteobacteria and Faecalibacterium, percentage of the short-chain fatty acid butyrate, psychiatric symptoms (Hospital Anxiety and Depression Scale), and biochemical liver variables." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31610228> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31610228_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31610228_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We included 28 patients with alcohol overconsumption (79% men), and 25 control patients (72% men)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31610228> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31662903_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31662903_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Faecal butyric acid was positively and negatively associated with the intake of starch (partial correlation = 0.264; <i>p</i>=0.015) and NNSs (partial correlation = -0.274; <i>p</i>=0.011), respectively." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31662903> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31685046_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31685046_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Shotgun metagenomics reveals both taxonomic and tryptophan pathway differences of gut microbiota in major depressive disorder patients." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/31685046> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31685046_12> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31685046_12" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Alterations of the gut microbiota may have the potential as biomarkers for distinguishing MDD patients form HCs." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31685046> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31685046_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31685046_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Most noteworthy, the MDD patients had increased levels of Bifidobacterium, which is commonly used as a probiotic." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31685046> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31704402_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31704402_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Here, in a randomised controlled experiment, we demonstrate that realistic exposures to trace-level dust from a high biodiversity soil can change mouse gut microbiota, in comparison to dust from low biodiversity soil or no soil (control) (n = 54 total mice, comprising 3 treatments × 18 mice, with 9 females + 9 males per group)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31704402> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31722343_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31722343_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The relationship between gut microbiota and the brain has gained attention in mental health due to the mounting evidence supporting the association of gut bacteria with mood and behavior." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31722343> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31722343_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31722343_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Patients with bipolar disorder exhibit an increased frequency of gastrointestinal illnesses such as inflammatory bowel disease, which mechanistically has been linked to microbial community function." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31722343> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31750916_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31750916_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Dietary fiber is a crucial component of a healthy diet, with benefits that can be attributed to processes in the gut microbiota and the resulting by-products." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31750916> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31750916_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31750916_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Further research into the link between dietary fiber intake and inflammation and depression is essential, as findings could potentially provide guidance for improvement in or prevention of inflammatory and depressive disorders." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31750916> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31769847_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31769847_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Probiotics and prebiotics: focus on psychiatric disorders - a systematic review." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/31769847> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31769847_12> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31769847_12" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Although recent findings in specific psychiatric disorders are encouraging, the use of prebiotics and probiotics in clinical practice stills lacks sufficiently robust evidence." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31769847> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31769847_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31769847_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This systematic review aims to find the existing clinical evidence that may justify the use of probiotics or prebiotics in psychiatric patients." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31769847> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31769847_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31769847_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "PRISMA guidelines were followed for a systematic literature review of randomized controlled trials that assessed the effect of prebiotics or probiotics in patients diagnosed with a classified psychiatric disorder." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31769847> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31940482_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31940482_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Recent discoveries have implicated the gut microbiome in the progression and severity of Parkinson's disease; however, how gut bacteria affect such neurodegenerative disorders remains unclear." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31940482> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31952911_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31952911_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Larger studies (especially of schizophrenia and major depressive disorder) are needed, but it is also of great importance to gather information of and control for factors that influence the result of a microbiota analysis including body mass index (BMI), smoking, alcohol consumption, diet habits, antibiotics, sample handling, wet laboratory methods and statistics." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31952911> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31955786_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31955786_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In addition to plant-origin and microbially-formed neuroactive compounds in foods, these substances are also formed by gut microbiota, which is the most attractive subject to assess the interaction between gut microbiota and mental health." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31955786> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32041265_11> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32041265_11" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Additionally, we observed a significant association between the gut microbiome diversity and the UPDRS III and the abundance of <i>Ruminococcaceae</i>." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32041265> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32041265_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32041265_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "16 PD patients underwent a well-controlled balanced, ovo-lacto vegetarian diet intervention including short fatty acids for 14 days." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32041265> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32056910_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32056910_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "A systematic review of the gut microbiota in anxiety/depression and irritable bowel syndrome." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32056910> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32056910_13> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32056910_13" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "These findings may inform the development of targeted treatment through the gut microbiota for individuals with both anxiety/depression and IBS." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32056910> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32056910_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32056910_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Background Anxiety/depression and irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) are highly prevalent and burdensome conditions, whose co-occurrence is estimated between 44 and 84%." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32056910> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32155131_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32155131_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Effects of the probiotic formulation SLAB51 in <i>in vitro</i> and <i>in vivo</i> Parkinson's disease models." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/32155131> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32155131_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32155131_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Parkinson is a common neurodegenerative disorder, characterized by motor and non-motor symptoms, including abnormalities in the gut function, which may appear before the motor sign." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32155131> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32163822_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32163822_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "However, the heterogeneity between studies precludes conclusions regarding differences in microbiota composition in mental disease and health and many of the studies are limited by a cross-sectional design, small sample sizes and multiple comparisons." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32163822> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32379622_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32379622_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Betaine supplementation is associated with the resilience in mice after chronic social defeat stress: a role of brain-gut-microbiota axis." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/32379622> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32379622_11> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32379622_11" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Interestingly, there are positive correlations between short-chain fatty acids (i.e., succinic acid, acetic acid, butyric acid) and several bacteria among the groups." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32379622> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32389857_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32389857_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "anxiety and depression) or on the development of pathologies affecting the CNS, such as autism spectrum disorders and neurodegenerative diseases (e.g." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32389857> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32431588_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32431588_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "To determine whether our compounds could inhibit brain-derived seeding activity, we utilized insoluble α-syn extracted from post-mortem MSA or PD brain specimens." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32431588> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32438623_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32438623_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Recipe for a Healthy Gut: Intake of Unpasteurised Milk Is Associated with Increased <i>Lactobacillus</i> Abundance in the Human Gut Microbiome." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/32438623> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32438623_14> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32438623_14" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "While concerns in relation to safety need to be considered, intake of unpasteurised milk and dairy products appear to be associated with the growth of the probiotic bacterial genus, <i>Lactobacillus</i>, in the human gut." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32438623> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32517799_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32517799_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Parkinson's disease (PD) is a systemic disease clinically defined by the degeneration of dopaminergic neurons in the brain." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32517799> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32517799_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32517799_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Eight genera and seven species changed significantly in their relative abundances between PD patients and healthy controls." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32517799> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32518376_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32518376_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The vagus nerve plays a role in the cross talk between the brain and gut microbiota, which could be involved in depression." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32518376> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32518376_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32518376_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The subdiaphragmatic vagus nerve serves as a major modulatory pathway between the brain and gut microbiota." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32518376> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32518376_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32518376_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In contrast, LPS did not produce a depression-like phenotype and downregulated synaptic proteins in the mPFC after SDV." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32518376> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32538869_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32538869_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This study emphasizes the possible role of the gut microbiome in modulation (and even initiation) of human neurodegenerative disorders, such as Parkinson's disease." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32538869> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32545788_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32545788_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Inflammation is a protective reaction activated in response to detrimental stimuli, such as dead cells, irritants or pathogens, by the evolutionarily conserved immune system and is regulated by the host." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32545788> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32545788_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32545788_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "It is so called because NLRP3 belongs to the family of nucleotide-binding and oligomerization domain-like receptors (NLRs)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32545788> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32572814_13> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32572814_13" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "These findings provide further support that butyrate or an agonist of FA3R may be of therapeutic potential in PD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32572814> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32600151_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32600151_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Alzheimer's disease (AD), the most common form of dementia, is a leading cause of death and a major cause of morbidity in older people." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32600151> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32600151_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32600151_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The gut microbiome has been increasingly implicated in the pathogenesis of several neurological diseases, including multiple sclerosis and Parkinson's disease." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32600151> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32600151_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32600151_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Furthermore, emerging evidence has demonstrated that there are alterations in gut microbiome composition in patients with AD, suggesting involvement of the microbiome-gut-brain axis." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32600151> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32739746_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32739746_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We used adolescent female mice in a gastrointestinal (GI) colonization model to demonstrate that the commensal fungus Candida albicans affects host health via the gut-brain axis." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32739746> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32739746_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32739746_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We demonstrated that C. albicans-colonized mice exhibited changes in the endocannabinoidome." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32739746> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32816830_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32816830_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Does Fibre-fix provided to people with irritable bowel syndrome who are consuming a low FODMAP diet improve their gut health, gut microbiome, sleep and mental health?" ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/32816830> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32816830_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32816830_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Multivariate analysis will be used to examine the gut microbiome and repeated measures Analysis of variance (ANOVA) will be used for dependent variables from questionnaires related to bowel symptoms, stool type, sleep, mental health and QOL to assess the differences between intervention and control groups after adjustment for confounding variables." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32816830> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32816830_14> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32816830_14" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "If Fibre-fix is shown to result in favourable changes in gut microbial composition, SCFA production, sleep and mental well-being without exacerbating symptoms, this will provide additional dietary management options for those with IBS following an LFD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32816830> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32816830_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32816830_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "A diet low in fermentable oligosaccharides, disaccharides, monosaccharides and polyols (FODMAP) is an effective way to reduce gut symptoms in people with irritable bowel syndrome (IBS)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32816830> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32816830_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32816830_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This study will examine the effect of Fibre-fix, a supplement containing a mix of dietary fibres, on the human gut microbiome composition, fermentative capacity, sleep, quality of life (QOL) and mental health of people with IBS who consume a low FODMAP diet (LFD)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32816830> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32819434_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32819434_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Autism spectrum disorder (ASD) is a developmental disorder, and the effective pharmacological treatments for the core autistic symptoms are currently limited." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32819434> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32819434_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32819434_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Increasing evidence, particularly that from clinical studies on ASD patients, suggests a functional link between the gut microbiota and the development of ASD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32819434> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32819434_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32819434_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Here, we found that the deletion of EphB6 induced autism-like behavior and disturbed the gut microbiota in mice." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32819434> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32890382_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32890382_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We searched in literature interactions between epigenetic processes and psychiatric disorders with a special interest for environmental factors such as traumatic or stress events, family relationships and also gut microbiota." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32890382> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32979562_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32979562_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The microbiome-gut-brain axis, especially the microbial tryptophan biosynthesis and metabolism pathway (MiTBamp), is closely connected to bipolar disorder with current major depressive episode (BPD)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32979562> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32979562_11> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32979562_11" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Alterations of microbes may have potential as biomarkers for distinguishing the BPD patients form HCs." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32979562> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32979562_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32979562_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Except for the microbiota taxa and MiTBamp analyses, we also built a classification model using the Random Forests (RF) and Boruta algorithm to find the microbial biomarkers for BPD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32979562> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32999308_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32999308_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "DJ-1 (Park7) affects the gut microbiome, metabolites and the development of innate lymphoid cells (ILCs)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/32999308> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32999308_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32999308_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In Parkinson's disease (PD) 85% of all patients experienced constipation many years before showing any signs of motor phenotypes." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32999308> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32999308_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32999308_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In the present study, we provide evidence that DJ-1 is implicated in shaping the gut microbiome including; their metabolite production, inflammation and innate immune cells (ILCs) development." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32999308> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32999308_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32999308_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In DJ-1 knock-out (DJ-1<sup>-/-</sup>) mice the production of fecal calprotectin and MCP-1 inflammatory proteins were elevated." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32999308> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33046051_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33046051_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This study examines the relationship between multiple sclerosis (MS), an autoimmune central nervous system disease, and gut microbial community composition, using the samples acquired by 16s rRNA sequencing technique." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33046051> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33063712_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33063712_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Different nutraceutical interventions have been devoted to normalizing gut microbiome dysbiosis and to improving biological outcomes in neurological conditions, including the use of probiotics." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33063712> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33063712_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33063712_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This review will discuss the potential use of probiotics for Parkinson's disease prevention or treatment or as adjuvant therapy, confirming that gut microbiota modulation influences different pro-survival pathways." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33063712> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33067915_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33067915_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Prenatal exposure to maternal immune activation (MIA) has been implicated as a risk factor for the development of autism spectrum disorder (ASD), though the conditions under which this elevated risk occurs are unclear." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33067915> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33067915_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33067915_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Animal literature demonstrates that antibiotic use, which affects the composition of the maternal gut microbiota, modifies the effect of MIA on neurodevelopmental outcomes in the offspring." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33067915> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33067915_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33067915_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The aim of this study was to assess whether antibiotic use during pregnancy modifies the association between MIA and subsequent risk of ASD, in a prospective birth cohort with 116 ASD cases and 860 typically developing (TD) child controls." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33067915> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33067915_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33067915_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "There was no evidence of interaction between fever or genitourinary infection and antibiotic use on the odds of ASD in unadjusted or adjusted analyzes." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33067915> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33067915_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33067915_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "However, we found evidence of an interaction between flu, specifically in second trimester, and antibiotic use at any point during pregnancy on the odds of ASD in the child." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33067915> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33067915_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33067915_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Among women who received an antibiotic during pregnancy, flu in trimester two was not associated with ASD (adjusted odds ratio [aOR] = 0.99 [0.43-2.28])." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33067915> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33067915_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33067915_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "These findings should be treated as hypothesis-generating and suggest that antibiotic use may modify the influence that MIA has on autism risk in the child." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33067915> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33076930_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33076930_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Here, we show that C. sporogenes deaminates levodopa, the main treatment in Parkinson's disease, and identify the aromatic aminotransferase responsible for the initiation of the deamination pathway." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33076930> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33177907_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33177907_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The gut microbiomes of insomnia patients compared with healthy controls were characterized by lower microbial richness and diversity, depletion of anaerobes, and short-chain fatty acid (SCFA)-producing bacteria, and an expansion of potential pathobionts." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33177907> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33194817_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33194817_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Multiomics Study of Gut Bacteria and Host Metabolism in Irritable Bowel Syndrome and Depression Patients." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/33194817> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33194817_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33194817_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In particular, diarrhea-predominant IBS (IBS-D) and depression exhibit similar fecal microbiota signatures, yet little is known about their pathogenic mechanism." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33194817> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33195226_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33195226_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Since the metabotropic glutamate receptor 5 (mGlu5) knockout mice provide a preclinical model of SZ with strong face and predictive validity, in the present study we performed gut microbiome profiling of mGlu5 knockout (KO) and wild-type (WT) mice by 16S rRNA sequencing of bacterial genomic DNA from fecal samples, analyzing bacterial diversity and taxonomic composition, as well as gastrointestinal parameters as indicators of gut function." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33195226> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33212907_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33212907_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "No significant between-group differences were seen in primary or secondary outcomes except for social functioning (<i>p</i> = 0.050) and mental health (<i>p</i> = 0.007) scores as improvements were seen in the probiotic group, but not in the placebo group." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33212907> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33271210_11> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33271210_11" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The main goal of this systematic review was to comprehensively examine and summarize the current evidence focused on the potential effect of the relationship between microbiota gut composition as well as the effects of probiotic supplementation on psychiatric disorders in children and adolescents." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33271210> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33271210_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33271210_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This review examined available evidence related to gut microbiota as well as the impact of probiotic supplementation on psychiatric disorders in the pediatric population reported to date." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33271210> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33271210_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33271210_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Another study suggested that prebiotic supplementation increased bifidobacterial populations for ASD and healthy controls." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33271210> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33271426_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33271426_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Growing evidence indicates the community of microorganisms throughout the gastrointestinal tract, (i.e., gut microbiota), is associated with anxiety and depressive disorders." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33271426> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33271426_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33271426_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We present the first systematic review of the gut microbiota in anxiety disorders, along with an update in depression." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33271426> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33271426_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33271426_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Systematic searches, following PRISMA guidelines, identified 26 studies (two case-control comparisons of the gut microbiota in generalised anxiety disorder, 18 in depression, one incorporating both anxiety/depression, and five including symptom-only measures)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33271426> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33271426_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33271426_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Several taxa, and their mechanisms of action, may relate to anxiety and depression pathophysiology via communication of peripheral inflammation to the brain." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33271426> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33301807_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33301807_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Furthermore, we discuss the research strategies that can be beneficial in this regard, including germ-free animals, fecal microbiota transplantation, probiotics, phages, and brain imaging techniques." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33301807> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33318317_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33318317_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Mental awareness improved mild cognitive impairment and modulated gut microbiome." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/33318317> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33327540_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33327540_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Within the array of biopsychosocial treatment modalities-including monoaminergic antidepressants, benzodiazepines, and CBT-there is an unmet need for the effective treatment of anxiety disorders resulting in full remission and recovery." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33327540> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33327540_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33327540_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Low-carbohydrate high-fat diets (LCHF) may provide a rewarding outcome for some anxiety disorders; more research is needed before this regimen can be recommended to patients on a daily basis, but the evidence mentioned in this paper should encourage researchers and clinicians to consider LCHF as a piece of advice somewhere between psychotherapy and pharmacology, or as an add-on to those two." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33327540> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33406628_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33406628_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The vermiform appendix is a lymphoid tissue in the cecum implicated in the storage and regulation of the gut microbiota." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33406628> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33406628_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33406628_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We then quantitatively measure changes in bile acid abundance in PD relative to the controls in the appendix (<i>n</i> = 15 PD, 12 C) and ileum (<i>n</i> = 20 PD, 20 C)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33406628> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33406628_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33406628_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Microbially derived toxic bile acids are heightened in PD, which suggests biliary abnormalities may play a role in PD pathogenesis." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33406628> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33422110_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33422110_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The impact of dextran sodium sulphate and probiotic pre-treatment in a murine model of Parkinson's disease." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/33422110> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33422110_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33422110_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Yet, neither DSS nor VSL#3 influenced the loss of substantia nigra dopamine neurons or the astrocytic and cytoskeleton remodeling protein changes that were provoked by the LPS followed by paraquat treatment." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33422110> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33422110_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33422110_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This could help explain the high degree of gastric disturbances in PD patients, as well as potentially be linked to the migration of peripheral inflammatory factors into the brain." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33422110> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33422110_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33422110_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We found that VSL#3 did not have any significant effects (beyond a blunting of LPS paraquat-induced weight loss)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33422110> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33454868_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33454868_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We also describe potential therapies to curtail the risk of breast cancer by restoring gut microbiota homeostasis and reducing systemic estrogen levels." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33454868> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33467657_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33467657_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Epidemiological, clinical and preclinical evidence suggests that maternal obesity, overnutrition and unhealthy dietary patterns programs have lasting adverse effects on the physical and mental health of offspring." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33467657> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33505487_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33505487_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "AMT could change the composition of gut microbiome which is associated with cytokines in CFC patients." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33505487> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33511258_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33511258_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "<i>plantarum</i> P-8, for 12 weeks could alleviate stress and anxiety of stressed adults." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33511258> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33514545_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33514545_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Human physiomimetic model integrating microphysiological systems of the gut, liver, and brain for studies of neurodegenerative diseases." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/33514545> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33514545_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33514545_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Of particular interest is the gut/microbiome-liver-brain axis for parsing out how genetic and environmental factors contribute to NDs." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33514545> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33514545_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33514545_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We have developed a mesofluidic platform technology to study gut-liver-cerebral interactions in the context of Parkinson's disease (PD)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33514545> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33677218_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33677218_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Rats showing depression-like behaviors induced by chronic unpredictable mild stress received fecal microbiota treatment or vehicle for 14 days, and alterations in behavior and neuroinflammation were assessed." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33677218> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33713734_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33713734_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Affective disorders impact prevalence of Flavonifractor and abundance of Christensenellaceae in gut microbiota." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/33713734> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33713734_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33713734_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In generalized linear models the CLR abundance of Christensenellaceae was lower in patients with AD (p = 0.024), and in smokers (p = 1.9*10<sup>-4</sup>), and inversely associated with increasing waist circumference (p = 0.031)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33713734> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33713734_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33713734_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The prevalence of Flavonifractor was higher in patients with AD (p = 0.033) and in smokers (p = 0.036)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33713734> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33713734_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33713734_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Unaffected relatives neither differed from patients with AD nor from healthy controls." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33713734> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33777957_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33777957_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "All the results strongly support that the brain neurotransmitter modulation by gut microbiota is indispensable to the physiopathology of anxiety and depression." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33777957> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33807447_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33807447_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "<i>Roseburia</i> and <i>Faecalibacterium</i> were increased in MD while being decreased in VD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33807447> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33819374_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33819374_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "TMA and its associated metabolites are produced by the human gut microbiome and have been suggested to serve as risk biomarkers for diabetes and cardiovascular diseases." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33819374> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33860090_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33860090_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "It has been postulated that gut pathogens and dysbiosis can contribute to peripheral inflammatory states or trigger downstream metabolic effects that exacerbate the neurodegenerative process in PD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33860090> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33860090_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33860090_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "However, the effects of probiotics on other PD aspects, such as motor disability and cognitive function, and its long-term efficacy (including effects on PD drug absorption in the gut) have not been investigated adequately." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33860090> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33895287_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33895287_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Chemotherapy treatment is associated with acute behavioral side effects (fatigue, anorexia) that significantly reduce patient quality of life and are dose-limiting, thereby increasing mortality (Kidwell et al., 2014)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33895287> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33895287_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33895287_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Our prior studies have demonstrated a correlation between chemotherapy treatment, gut changes, peripheral and central inflammation, and behavioral symptoms in mice." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33895287> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33899052_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33899052_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The gut microbiome appears to be predictive of Parkinson's disease (PD) with constipation." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33899052> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33899052_14> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33899052_14" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Changes in the gut microbiome Post-OMM were associated with UPDRS results and constipation measures." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33899052> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33899052_15> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33899052_15" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Clinical trials and studies to develop the gut microbiome into a validated biomarker for PD are necessary to understand the impact of OMM in patients with PD and constipation." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33899052> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33899052_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33899052_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "An osteopathic manipulative medicine (OMM) sequence used physical exam assessment and manual treatment of neuromusculoskeletal dysfunctions pertinent to constipation in PD for this prospective ABA-design study, IRB-NYITBHS1065." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33899052> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33936013_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33936013_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Here, we investigated GABA production by <i>Bacteroides</i> in culture and metabolic assays combined with comparative genomics and phylogenetics." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33936013> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33936013_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33936013_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Using the model organism <i>Bacteroides thetaiotaomicron</i> DSM 2079, we determined GABA production kinetics, its impact on milieu pH, and we assessed its role in mitigating acid-induced cellular damage." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33936013> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33938181_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33938181_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Human glucose-dependent insulinotropic polypeptide (GIP) is an antimicrobial adjuvant re-sensitising multidrug-resistant Gram-negative bacteria." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/33938181> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33938181_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33938181_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Increasing antibiotic resistance in Gram-negative bacteria has mandated the development of both novel antibiotics and alternative therapeutic strategies." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33938181> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33938181_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33938181_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The effect was comparable to bacterial mutants lacking the inner and outer membrane efflux pump factor proteins AcrB and TolC." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33938181> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33938181_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33938181_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "While GIP was devoid of direct antimicrobial activity, it has a potent membrane depolarizing effect, and at low concentrations, it significantly potentiated the activity of eight antibiotics and bile salt by reducing MICs by 4-8-fold" ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33938181> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33963281_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33963281_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Gut microbiota modulates the inflammatory response and cognitive impairment induced by sleep deprivation." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/33963281> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33963281_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33963281_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The present study investigated the impact of SD on gut microbiota composition and explored whether alterations of the gut microbiota play a causal role in chronic inflammatory states and cognitive impairment that are induced by SD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33963281> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33963281_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33963281_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "These findings indicate that gut dysbiosis contributes to both peripheral and central inflammatory processes and cognitive deficits that are induced by SD, which may open avenues for potential interventions that can relieve the detrimental consequences of sleep loss." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33963281> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33963284_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33963284_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "However, an increasing number of preclinical studies show that arketamine has greater potency and longer-lasting antidepressant-like effects than esketamine in rodents, despite the lower binding affinity of arketamine for the NMDAR." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33963284> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33967849_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33967849_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "There were no differences between probiotics and control groups in global mental health scores at end of follow-up (MD 1.09; 95% CI -2.04, 4.22)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33967849> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33967849_13> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33967849_13" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "More research is needed before prebiotics, probiotics, and synbiotics are recommended to support maternal mental health and well-being in the perinatal period." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33967849> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33967849_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33967849_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Although statistical significance was not achieved, probiotics showed an advantage in the proportion of participants scoring below an established cut-off for depression (pOR 0.68; 95% CI 0.43, 1.07)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33967849> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34002020_13> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34002020_13" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Faecal, but not serum, levels of the endocannabinoid palmitoylethanolamide (PEA) mediated this association: the indirect effect was significant (β = -0.13; 95%CI: -0.24 to -0.01; P = 0.03), as was the total effect (β = -0.38; 95%CI: -0.72 to -0.04; P = 0.03), whereas the direct effect of alpha diversity on anhedonia/amotivation was attenuated fully (β = -0.25; 95%CI: -0.60 to 0.09; P = 0.16)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34002020> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34002020_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34002020_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The model was set using alpha diversity (within-individual gut-microbial diversity) as predictor, serum and faecal levels of the endocannabinoid palmitoylethanolamide (PEA) as mediator, and anhedonia/amotivation as outcome." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34002020> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34032650_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34032650_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Several studies of psychobiotics (bacteria with a potential mental health benefit) have been conducted in healthy populations and in patients with depression." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34032650> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34098340_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34098340_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Taxa from butyrate-producing families, Lachnospiraceae and Ruminococcaceae, were more abundant in mothers of children with normative behaviour." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34098340> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34147969_12> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34147969_12" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "These findings suggest that F. rodentium might contribute to the conversion of resilient Ephx2 KO mice into KO mice with depression-like phenotypes." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34147969> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34147969_13> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34147969_13" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The brain-gut-microbiota axis via the subdiaphragmatic vagus nerve plays a crucial role in susceptibility and resilience to stress." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34147969> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34147969_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34147969_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Ephx2 knock-out (KO) mice exposed to chronic social defeat stress (CSDS) did not show depression-like behaviors, indicating stress resilience." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34147969> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34147969_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34147969_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Here we examined whether the brain-gut-microbiota axis influences the resilience in Ephx2 KO mice." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34147969> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34172092_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34172092_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Depletion of acetate-producing bacteria from the gut microbiota facilitates cognitive impairment through the gut-brain neural mechanism in diabetic mice." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/34172092> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34172092_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34172092_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We found that vancomycin exposure disrupted the gut microbiome, altered host metabolic phenotypes, and facilitated cognitive impairment in T1D mice." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34172092> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34172092_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34172092_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Long-term acetate deficiency due to depletion of acetate-producing bacteria resulted in the reduction of synaptophysin (SYP) in the hippocampus as well as learning and memory impairments." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34172092> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34174901_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34174901_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We found that minocycline had a profound acute effect on the microbiota diversity and composition, which was paralleled by the subsequent normalization of spinal cord injury-induced suppression of cytokines/chemokines." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34174901> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34174901_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34174901_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Importantly, gut dysbiosis following spinal cord injury has been linked to the development of anxiety-like behavior, which was also decreased by minocycline." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34174901> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34204057_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34204057_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Moreover, the MD may further contribute to the improvement of reproductive health, modify the risk for neurodegenerative diseases, and protect against depression and psychosocial maladjustment." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34204057> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34205336_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34205336_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We also discuss how microbiome dysbiosis affects cognitive function, especially in neurodegenerative diseases such as Alzheimer's disease and Parkinson's disease." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34205336> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34216356_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34216356_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In addition, aging and neurodegenerative diseases, including Alzheimer's disease and Parkinson's disease, have become topics of intense interest in biomedical research." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34216356> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34277527_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34277527_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Some nutritional deficiencies and gut microbiota alterations have been linked to NDDs, suggesting their potential pathogenic implications." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34277527> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34290352_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34290352_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The change of gut microbiota in MDD patients under SSRIs treatment." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/34290352> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34290352_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34290352_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The purpose of this study was to investigate the changes of intestinal microbiota in depressed patients after antidepressant treatment." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34290352> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34311029_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34311029_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Both age and AD share common metabolic hallmarks such as increased oxidative stress and perturbed metabolic function, and age remains the most strongly correlated risk factor for AD, a neurodegenerative disease." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34311029> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34311029_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34311029_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The brain lipid profile can be influenced directly with dietary administration of lipids themselves, although because of synergistic effects of nutrients it may be more useful to consider a multi-component diet rather than single nutrient supplementation." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34311029> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34311029_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34311029_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Gut microbiota also serve as a source of beneficial lipids, and the value of treatments that manipulate the composition of gut microbiome should not be ignored." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34311029> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34357554_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34357554_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In this review, we have discussed how the gut microbiota-mediated immune response inclines the host physiology towards neurodegeneration and indicated the gut microbiota as a potential future candidate for the management of neurodegenerative disorders." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34357554> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34393849_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34393849_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Association Between Abundance of <i>Haemophilus</i> in the Gut Microbiota and Negative Symptoms of Schizophrenia." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/34393849> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34399524_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34399524_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Dietary advanced glycation endproducts (AGEs) increase their concentration in plasma and tissues, result in inflammation and modulate gut microbial composition in mice; evidence for reversibility." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/34399524> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34399524_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34399524_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Dietary advanced glycation endproducts (AGEs) are associated with negative biological effects, possibly due to accumulation in plasma and tissues and through modulation of inflammation and gut microbiota." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34399524> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34399524_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34399524_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "After 10 weeks of baked chow, a substantial panel of AGEs were increased in plasma, liver, and kidney." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34399524> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34422393_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34422393_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "A discussion of the gut microbiome's development, determinants, and dysbiosis in cancers of the esophagus and stomach." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/34422393> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34422393_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34422393_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "It is important to understand the nature of the gastrointestinal tract microbiome and its potentional risk factors for dysbiosis in order to tailor its application to the individual patient and create an era of highly personalized, precision medicine." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34422393> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34422879_14> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34422879_14" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Numerous studies on the role of different micronutrients (omega-3 fatty acids, bioactive polyphenols from fruit and medicinal plants) in the prevention, prediction, and treatment of NDD have been conducted, but we are still far away from a personalized diet plan for individual NDD patients." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34422879> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34422879_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34422879_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Typical for NDD are the malfunctioning of neurons and their irreversible loss, which often progress irreversibly to dementia and ultimately to death." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34422879> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34437440_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34437440_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Association of Polygenic Risk Score and Bacterial Toxins at Screening Colonoscopy with Colorectal Cancer Progression: A Multicenter Case-Control Study." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/34437440> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34437440_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34437440_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Our results showed that CIF toxin is associated with polyps or adenomas, whereas pks+ seems to be a predisposing factor for CRC." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34437440> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34444820_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34444820_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Furthermore, NVP-1704 increased <i>Bifidobacteriaceae</i> and <i>Lactobacillacea</i>, whereas it decreased <i>Enterobacteriaceae</i> in the gut microbiota composition." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34444820> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34520319_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34520319_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This review will provide an evaluation of clinical and animal studies describing GM alterations in distinct conditions, including AD, sleep and circadian disruption." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34520319> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34560239_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34560239_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The data suggest that MPTP-induced increases in colonic p-α-Syn expression might be associated with dopaminergic neurotoxicity in the striatum via gut-microbiota-brain axis." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34560239> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34560239_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34560239_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "There was a negative correlation between the expression of TH in the striatum and the expression of p-α-Syn in the colon, suggesting a role of gut-brain communication." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34560239> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34560239_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34560239_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Furthermore, the relative abundance of the genus Faecalicatena in the MPTP-treated group was significantly lower than that of control group." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34560239> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34576000_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34576000_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Parkinson's disease (PD) is currently the second most common neurodegenerative disorder, burdening about 10 million elderly individuals worldwide." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34576000> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34576833_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34576833_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Here, we show substantial microbiota changes that were associated with oxytocin administration and the decreased anxiety/depression-like behaviors it conferred in a rat model of corticosterone-induced stress." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34576833> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34589800_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34589800_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In this short review, an overview of inflammatory and gut microbiota status in human depression and in rodent models of the illness are provided." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34589800> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34589800_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34589800_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Finally, dietary interventions targeting the gut microbiota-immune-brain axis in the context of depression are briefly discussed." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34589800> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34692176_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34692176_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "<b>Objective:</b> Inflammatory bowel diseases (IBDs) are complex chronic inflammatory disorders of the gastro-intestinal (GI) tract with uncertain etiology." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34692176> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34692176_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34692176_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Studies evaluating any possible associations between gut microbiome, psychological state, immune modulation, and autonomic function with IBDs were identified." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34692176> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34704023_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34704023_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We performed an exhaustive review of the literature to identify original published clinical studies including 16S rRNA gene sequencing on Parkinson's disease, multiple Sclerosis and Alzheimer's disease." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34704023> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34758889_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34758889_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The hippocampal synaptic ultrastructure was damaged in FD mice, characterized by widened synaptic clefts and thinned postsynaptic densities." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34758889> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34776854_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34776854_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "<b>Conclusion:</b> This study provides the first comprehensive characterization of the gut microbiome and predicted functional metabolic effects in a southern hemisphere PD population, further exploring the possible mechanisms whereby the gut microbiota may exert their influence on this disease, and providing evidence for the incorporation of such data in future individualized therapeutic strategies." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34776854> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34776854_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34776854_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The present study characterized the gut microbiota and associated changes in host metabolic pathways in an Australian cohort of people with PD (PwP)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34776854> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34776854_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34776854_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Illumina sequencing of the V3 and V4 regions of the 16S rRNA gene was used to distinguish inter-cohort differences in gut microbiota; KEGG analysis was subsequently performed to predict functional changes in host metabolic pathways." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34776854> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34830610_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34830610_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Overwhelming evidence demonstrates an important role of the gut microbiome in the development of a wide range of diseases, including obesity, metabolic disorders, and mental health symptoms." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34830610> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34830610_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34830610_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Given that obesity and mental health symptoms are both hallmarks of Prader-Willi syndrome, targeting the gut microbiome may be a promising therapeutical strategy." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34830610> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34836918_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34836918_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Footprints of a microbial toxin from the gut microbiome to mesencephalic mitochondria." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/34836918> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34836918_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34836918_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "These events primed neuroinflammation, dopaminergic neuronal loss and motor deficits." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34836918> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34870091_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34870091_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Compositional and functional alterations in the oral and gut microbiota in patients with psychosis or schizophrenia: A systematic review." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/34870091> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34870091_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34870091_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Emerging evidence suggests that the composition and/or function of intestinal microbiome differs in those with psychosis and schizophrenia as compared with controls." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34870091> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34884399_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34884399_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Differences in the Composition of Gut Microbiota between Patients with Parkinson's Disease and Healthy Controls: A Cohort Study." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/34884399> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34884399_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34884399_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Gut microbiome and colonic inflammation can be associated with the predisposition and progression of Parkinson's disease (PD)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34884399> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34884399_12> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34884399_12" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In conclusion, the patients diagnosed with PD have significantly different gut microbiota profiles in comparison with healthy controls." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34884399> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34884399_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34884399_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The presented study aimed to compare gastrointestinal microbiota composition between patients diagnosed with PD and treated only with Levodopa to healthy controls." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34884399> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34970638_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34970638_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Compared with CON mice, CUMS-exposed mice showed a significant increase in both α and β diversity." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34970638> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34970638_12> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34970638_12" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "DEX-treated mice had a decrease in the abundance of <i>Clostridium XVIII</i>." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34970638> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34970638_13> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34970638_13" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Levels of occludin in colon tissue of DEX-treated mice were reduced." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34970638> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34988495_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34988495_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Characterization of the gut microbiota among Veterans with unique military-related exposures and high prevalence of chronic health conditions: A United States-Veteran Microbiome Project (US-VMP) study." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/34988495> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34988495_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34988495_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "United States (US) military Veterans are a unique population in that their military-related exposures can have consequences for both physical and mental health, but the gut microbiome of this population has been understudied." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34988495> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34988495_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34988495_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We found that PVD and cardiovascular disease were associated with lower microbiota diversity in the gut (i.e., α-diversity), while supplemental vitamin use was associated with higher α-diversity." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34988495> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34988495_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34988495_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Our study contributes novel insights as to whether the unique exposures of Veterans in this cohort correlate with gut microbiota characteristics and, in line with previous findings with other population-level studies of the microbiome, confirms associations between numerous health conditions and medications with the gut microbiome." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34988495> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35083314_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35083314_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Gut microbiome changes have been associated with human ageing and implicated in age-related diseases including Alzheimer's disease and Parkinson's disease." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35083314> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35207632_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35207632_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Abnormalities in the gastrointestinal (GI) tract of Parkinson's disease (PD) sufferers were first reported over 200 years ago; however, the extent and role of GI dysfunction in PD disease progression is still unknown." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35207632> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35281490_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35281490_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Mechanistic Insights Into Gut Microbiome Dysbiosis-Mediated Neuroimmune Dysregulation and Protein Misfolding and Clearance in the Pathogenesis of Chronic Neurodegenerative Disorders." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/35281490> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35281490_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35281490_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "These can further disrupt intestinal barrier permeability, aggravate the systemic pro-inflammatory state, impair blood-brain barrier permeability and recruit immune mediators leading to neuroinflammation and neurodegeneration." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35281490> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35281490_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35281490_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Conversely, microbial dysbiosis - defined as alterations in richness and relative abundances - of the gut is implicated in the pathogenesis of several chronic neurological and neurodegenerative disorders." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35281490> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35327401_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35327401_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The fruit fly, <i>Drosophila melanogaster</i>, is a valuable animal model for studying host-gut microbiota interactions in translational aspects." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35327401> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35432226_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35432226_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This may further elucidate the impact of the gut microbiome in Parkinson's disease and show how it may not be homogenous across individuals with Parkinson's disease." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35432226> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35571084_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35571084_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Emerging evidence from both clinical studies and animal models indicates the importance of the interaction between the gut microbiome and the brain in the pathogenesis of neurodegenerative diseases (NDs)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35571084> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35571084_11> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35571084_11" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Whether these potential therapeutics indeed protect neurons from proteotoxicity by inhibiting the cross-seeding between bacterial and human amyloid proteins awaits further investigations." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35571084> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35674870_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35674870_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Neurodegeneration and Neuroinflammation in Parkinson's Disease: a Self-Sustained Loop." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/35674870> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35674870_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35674870_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Whatever the original trigger of neuroinflammation in PD, what appears quite clear is that the aberrant activation of glial cells and other components of the immune system creates a vicious circle in which neurodegeneration and neuroinflammation nourish each other." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35674870> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35722294_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35722294_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We found that <i>Blautia</i> was the unique genus consistently depleted across feces, blood, and brain samples of PD patients (<i>P</i> < 0.05), despite using rigorous criteria to remove contaminants." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35722294> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35722294_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35722294_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Through the integration of microbiome and transcriptome, our study depicted microbial profiles in the feces, blood, and brain of PD patients, and identified <i>Blautia</i> genus as a potential genus linked to PD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35722294> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35798742_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35798742_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Although several studies have identified a distinct gut microbial composition in Parkinson's disease (PD), few studies have investigated the oral microbiome or functional alteration of the microbiome in PD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35798742> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35798742_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35798742_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Oral Lactobacillus was more abundant in PD patients and was associated with opportunistic pathogens in the gut (FDR-adjusted P < 0.038)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35798742> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35914559_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35914559_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Microbial alterations within the gut microbiome appear to be a common feature of individuals with Parkinson's disease (PD), providing further evidence for the role of the gut-brain axis in PD development." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35914559> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35914559_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35914559_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "From these experimental data, we postulate that TCE exposure within contaminated drinking water could induce alterations of the gut microbiome that contributes to chronic disease risk, including idiopathic PD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35914559> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35965349_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35965349_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Systematic profiling of the chicken gut microbiome reveals dietary supplementation with antibiotics alters expression of multiple microbial pathways with minimal impact on community structure." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/35965349> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35965349_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35965349_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The emergence of antimicrobial resistance is a major threat to global health and has placed pressure on the livestock industry to eliminate the use of antibiotic growth promotants (AGPs) as feed additives." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35965349> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35965349_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35965349_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Birds were raised under two different diets and AGP treatments, and 16S rDNA surveys applied to six GI sites sampled at three key timepoints of the poultry life cycle." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35965349> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36056574_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36056574_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "A Pilot Study of the Gut Microbiota Associated With Depressive Symptoms and Sleep Disturbance Among Chinese and Korean Immigrants in the United States." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/36056574> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36056574_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36056574_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Examine associations of the GM with depressive symptoms and sleep disturbance among Chinese and Korean American immigrants." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36056574> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36072564_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36072564_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The macrophages residing in the brain comprise parenchymal microglia and non-parenchymal macrophages located in the perivascular spaces, meninges, and the choroid plexus." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36072564> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36072680_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36072680_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) is a functional gastrointestinal disorder leading to chronic debilitating issues." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36072680> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36191806_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36191806_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "A role of gut-microbiota-brain axis via subdiaphragmatic vagus nerve in depression-like phenotypes in Chrna7 knock-out mice." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/36191806> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36191806_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36191806_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The α7 subtype of the nicotinic acetylcholine receptor (α7 nAChR: coded by Chrna7) is known to regulate the cholinergic ascending anti-inflammatory pathway." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36191806> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36191806_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36191806_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "There were several genus and species altered among the three groups [wild-type (WT) + sham group, KO + sham group, KO + SDV group]." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36191806> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36216056_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36216056_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Epidemiological evidence reported that particulate matter (PM) was associated with increased schizophrenia (SCZ) risk." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36216056> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36216056_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36216056_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "However, it remains unclear whether PM induces SCZ-like symptoms and how gut microbiome regulates them." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36216056> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36332796_12> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36332796_12" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "However, there is a significant unmet need for randomized clinical trials to investigate the effectiveness of microbial products, probiotic-based supplementation, and dietary intervention in reversing gut microbial dysbiosis in PD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36332796> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36332796_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36332796_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Both enteric and central nervous systems have been implicated in the pathogenesis of sporadic PD, thus highlighting the crosstalk between the gut and brain." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36332796> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36346385_12> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36346385_12" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "These studies uncover a novel microglia-dependent interaction between diet and motor symptoms in mice, findings that may have implications for neuroinflammation and PD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36346385> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36346385_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36346385_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Most cases of PD are non-hereditary, suggesting a strong role for environmental factors, and it has been speculated that disease may originate in peripheral tissues such as the gastrointestinal (GI) tract before affecting the brain." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36346385> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36346385_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36346385_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The gut microbiome is altered in PD and may impact motor and GI symptoms as indicated by animal studies, although mechanisms of gut-brain interactions remain incompletely defined." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36346385> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36346385_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36346385_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We therefore investigated whether a fiber-rich diet influences microglial function in α-synuclein overexpressing (ASO) mice, a preclinical model with PD-like symptoms and pathology." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36346385> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36346385_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36346385_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Feeding a prebiotic high-fiber diet attenuates motor deficits and reduces α-synuclein aggregation in the substantia nigra of mice." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36346385> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36411639_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36411639_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This study is also focused on major metagenomic approaches and their role in gut microbes characterization." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36411639> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36411639_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36411639_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Gut microbes cause several types of gastrointestinal diseases like ulcer stomach and intestine and irritable bowel syndrome." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36411639> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36411639_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36411639_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Metagenomics has been employed for the identification, and characterization of gut microbes and microbial-derived metabolites." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36411639> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36411639_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36411639_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This review is focused on the gut microbes-brain relationship and the role of gut microbes in neurodegenerative diseases." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36411639> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36462169_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36462169_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We hypothesized that gut leakage of microbial products due to intestinal inflammation could contribute to systemic inflammasome activation in SMI." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36462169> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36462169_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36462169_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We assessed associations with plasma IL-18 and IL-18BPa and leukocyte mRNA expression of NLRP3 and NLRC4 as markers of inflammasome activation." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36462169> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36462169_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36462169_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Our findings support that intestinal barrier inflammation and dysfunction in SMI could contribute to systemic inflammation through inflammasome activation." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36462169> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36493975_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36493975_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Notably, there were correlations between demyelination or microglial activation in the brain and the relative abundance of several microbiome populations, suggesting a link between gut microbiota and the brain." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36493975> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36532064_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36532064_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We further suggest that changes of the BrainBiota during brain diseases may be the consequence or cause of the chronic inflammation similarly to the gut microbiota." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36532064> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36550591_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36550591_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Antidepression of Xingpijieyu formula targets gut microbiota derived from depressive disorder." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/36550591> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36550591_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36550591_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This investigation aims to determine the antidepressant role of Xingpijieyu formula (XPJYF) mediated via gut microbiota (GM)-brain axis." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36550591> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36550591_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36550591_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The behaviors were studied by forced swimming test, open field test, sucrose preference test, and body weight." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36550591> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36564391_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36564391_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In this study, the largest meta-analysis currently of the gut microbiome in PD was analyzed, including 2269 samples by 16S rRNA gene and 236 samples by shotgun metagenomics, aiming to reveal the connection between PD and gut microbiome and establish a model to predict PD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36564391> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36564391_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36564391_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "These changes may lead to a decrease in potential anti-inflammatory substances (short-chain fatty acids) and an increase in potential pro-inflammatory substances (lipopolysaccharides, hydrogen sulfide and glutamate)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36564391> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36651663_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36651663_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The gut-microbiota-brain axis in a Spanish population in the aftermath of the COVID-19 pandemic: microbiota composition linked to anxiety, trauma, and depression profiles." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/36651663> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36698474_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36698474_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Compared with the USA and the world, the Chinese neurological and mental disorders DALY percent was least in the generation over 75 but rapidly increased in younger generations and surpassed the USA and/or the world in the last decades." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36698474> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36699448_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36699448_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Our study applied linear discriminant analysis (LDA) effect size (LEfSe) and genome-wide association analysis in the cohort with both gut sequencing data and genomics data." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36699448> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36699448_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36699448_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "<i>Actinobacteria</i> and <i>Pseudomonades</i> were found more in the MDD group." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36699448> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36738999_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36738999_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Neuropsychiatric disorders, including anxiety and depression, are one of the most common mental illnesses worldwide." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36738999> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36738999_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36738999_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Glucose intolerance and liver fat were detected by IGTT and liver lipid kit." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36738999> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36757367_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Correcting this imbalance with medicinal herbs, the metabolic products of dysregulated bacteria and probiotics have shown hope for the treatment of these neuronal disorders." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36757367> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36757367_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In this regard, we focus on irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) given its strong links to brain function and anxiety disorders." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36757367> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_12> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36760344_12" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "According to the LEfSe analysis, two beneficial bacterial genera (<i>Megamonas</i> and <i>Faecalibacterium</i>) were significantly enriched in the meditation group." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36760344> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_17> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36760344_17" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The microbiota enriched in monks was associated with a reduced risk of anxiety, depression and cardiovascular disease and could enhance immune function." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36760344> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36794003_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36794003_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "High-fiber diet ameliorates gut microbiota, serum metabolism and emotional mood in type 2 diabetes patients." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/36794003> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36794003_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36794003_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Here, we conducted a randomized clinical study to analyze the changes in gut microbiota, serum metabolism and emotional mood of patients with T2DM after consumption of a high-fiber diet." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36794003> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36794003_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36794003_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Therefore, the current study demonstrated that the intestinal microbiota alterations which were influenced by the high-fiber diet could improve the serum metabolism and emotional mood of patients with T2DM." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36794003> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36900437_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Several studies concluded that <i>Lactobacillus plantarum</i> is a GABA-producing bacteria and can alleviate depression." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36900437> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36900437_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The chronic unpredictable mild stress (CUMS) model was established in rats, and these rats were treated with FWG for four weeks to evaluate the effects of FWG in relieving depression." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36900437> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36931666_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Effect of date seed (<i>Phoenix dactylifera</i>) supplementation as functional food on cardiometabolic risk factors, metabolic endotoxaemia and mental health in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus: a blinded randomised controlled trial protocol." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/36931666> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36931666_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This study protocol will be conducted as randomised, triple-blind, placebo-controlled trial with the inclusion of 48 patients with T2DM." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36931666> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36938477_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Evaluating the effectiveness of probiotics in relieving constipation in Parkinson's disease: A systematic review and meta-analysis." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/36938477> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36938477_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Constipation is a common complaint reported by PD patients." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36938477> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36978911_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The Potential of Flavonoids and Flavonoid Metabolites in the Treatment of Neurodegenerative Pathology in Disorders of Cognitive Decline." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/36978911> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36978911_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Certain food items have been identified with high prebiotic profiles suggesting that neutraceutical supplementation may be beneficially employed to preserve a healthy population of bacterial symbiont species and minimize the establishment of harmful pathogenic organisms." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36978911> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36978911_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Bioconversion of dietary flavonoid components in the gut generates therapeutic metabolites that can also be transported by the vagus nerve and systemic circulation to brain cell populations to exert a beneficial effect." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36978911> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36989335_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36989335_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Multinutrients may benefit children with ADHD and irritability regardless of overall diet quality." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36989335> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37049591_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Dysbiosis of the Gut Microbiota and Kynurenine (Kyn) Pathway Activity as Potential Biomarkers in Patients with Major Depressive Disorder." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37049591> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37049591_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "However, gut microbiota changes in major depressive disorder (MDD) patients and their association with disease mechanisms remain undefined." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37049591> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37049591_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Fifty MDD patients and sixty healthy controls were recruited from the Shanghai Healthy Mental Center, China." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37049591> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37071196_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Therefore, the current preregistered study ( https://osf.io/8ymav , September 7, 2022) described child gut microbiota development in the first 14 years of life and explored its relations to internalizing and externalizing difficulties and social anxiety in puberty, a period of high relevance for the development of mental health problems." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37071196> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37071196_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "These three clusters were compositionally similar to enterotypes (i.e., a robust classification of the gut microbiota based on its composition across different populations) enriched in Bacteroides, Prevotella, and Ruminococcus, respectively." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37071196> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37071196_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Two Prevotella 9-predominated clusters, including one reported by us earlier in middle childhood and the other one in puberty, were associated with more externalizing behavior at age 14." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37071196> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37095530_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Herein, we used the \"Lunar Palace 365\" mission, a 1-year-long isolation study in the Lunar Palace 1 (a closed manned Bioregenerative Life Support System facility with excellent performance), to investigate the correlation between gut microbiota and psychological changes, in order to find some new potential psychobiotics to maintain and improve the psychological health of crew members." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37095530> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37156128_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Comparison of gut microbiome profile in patients with schizophrenia and healthy controls - A plausible non-invasive biomarker?" ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37156128> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37168424_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37168424_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Features of gut microbiota and short-chain fatty acids in patients with first-episode depression and their relationship with the clinical symptoms." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37168424> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37168424_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37168424_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The abundance of <i>Parasutterella</i> in the MDD group was higher than that in the C group." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37168424> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37207228_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37207228_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In addition to their established role in innate immunity throughout the body, research is increasingly showing that the Toll-like receptor 2 and Toll-like receptor 4 signaling pathways shape the development and function of the gut and enteric nervous system." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37207228> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37209162_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Bacillus licheniformis prevents and reduces anxiety-like and depression-like behaviours." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37209162> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37209162_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "KEY POINTS: • B. licheniformis reduced depressive-like and anxiety-like behaviours induced by the chronic unpredictable mild stress." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37209162> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37209162_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Bacillus licheniformis is a probiotic used to treat gut diseases through balancing the gut microbiome during lasting years." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37209162> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37209162_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We found that B. licheniformis reduced the depressive-like and anxiety-like behaviours of the rats during the CUMS process." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37209162> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37212075_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37212075_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Parkinson's disease is a heterogeneous neurodegenerative disorder with distinctive gut microbiome patterns suggesting that interventions targeting the gut microbiota may prevent, slow, or reverse disease progression and severity." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37212075> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37212075_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37212075_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "IgA-Biome analyses identified significant alpha and beta diversity differences between the Parkinson's disease phenotypes and the Firmicutes/Bacteroides ratio was significantly higher in those with TD compared to those with AR." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37212075> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37368331_38> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37368331_38" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "(4) Conclusion: A significant gut dysbiosis, involving multiple bacterial taxa, was found in PD patients compared to healthy people in the occidental regions." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37368331> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37377497_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37377497_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In response to environmental challenges, stress is a common reaction, but dysregulation of the stress response can lead to neuropsychiatric disorders, including depression and cognitive impairment." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37377497> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37377497_13> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37377497_13" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Moreover, well-designed clinical trials are needed to increase the scientific validity of triphala polyphenols' beneficial effects for preventing and treating cognitive impairment and psychological dysfunction." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37377497> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37396336_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37396336_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Although the prevalence of depression and anxiety in women is about twice that of men, very few studies have examined whether physical exercise could affect mental health differently according to sex." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37396336> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37396336_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37396336_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This study examined, in singly-housed mice, the sex-specific effects of voluntary exercise on depressive- and anxiety-like behaviors as well as on different markers along the gut microbiota-immune-brain axis." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37396336> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37400971_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37400971_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The analysis revealed a significant effect size (SMD = -0.51, 95% CI = -0.79 to -0.22, <i>p</i> < .001, T2 = 0.54, I2 = 79.85%), indicating that MMD might provoke behavioral impairments in the adult offspring." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37400971> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37400971_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37400971_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Therefore, experimental perinatal MMD is vertically transmitted to the offspring, negatively impacting behavioral parameters related to psychiatric disorders." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37400971> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37403161_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37403161_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Braak's hypothesis states that sporadic Parkinson's disease (PD) follows a specific progression of pathology from the peripheral to the central nervous system, and this progression can be monitored by detecting the accumulation of alpha-Synuclein (α-Syn) protein." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37403161> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37403161_11> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37403161_11" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The dynamics of Lactobacillus and Alistipes were monitored and reduced Lactobacillus and increased Alistipes abundance was discerned in ageing TG rats." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37403161> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37403161_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37403161_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Immunohistochemistry and immunofluorescence imaging were applied to detect the α-Syn protein." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37403161> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37449597_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37449597_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Gut-microbiome-brain axis: the crosstalk between the vagus nerve, alpha-synuclein and the brain in Parkinson's disease." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37449597> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37468912_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37468912_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Dysregulation of gut microbiota-host bile acid (BA) co-metabolism is a critical pathogenic factor of diarrhea-predominant irritable bowel syndrome (IBS-D)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37468912> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37468912_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37468912_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM), instructed by pattern differentiation, is effective in treating IBS-D, in which liver depression and spleen deficiency (LDSD) is the most prevalent pattern." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37468912> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37469436_11> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37469436_11" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In summary, we utilized a comparative approach to delineate differences between PS150 and GR1009 and proposed that EPS may serve as a key factor that mediates the observed hypnotic effect." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37469436> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37469436_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37469436_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Our comparative genomics analysis also revealed distinct genetic characteristics in EPS biosynthesis between GR1009 and PS150." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37469436> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37481569_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37481569_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Study of the gut microbiome in Egyptian patients with Parkinson's Disease." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37481569> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37571393_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37571393_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Although phytochemicals have shown promise in slowing down the progression of age-related brain diseases, more studies to identify their efficacy, alone or in combinations, in preclinical systems can help to design novel nutritional strategies for the management of neurodegenerative diseases in humans." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37571393> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37574818_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37574818_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Here, we evaluated the effect of oral ingestion of live and inactivated Lactobacillus plantarum CCFM8661 on oleic acid-induced acne using a mouse model." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37574818> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37577447_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37577447_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The association between oral and gut microbiota in male patients with alcohol dependence." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37577447> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37577447_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37577447_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The current study aimed to explore the association between oral and gut microbiota in AD to clarify whether oral microbiota could ectopically colonize into the gut." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37577447> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37577447_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37577447_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The α-diversity of oral microbiota and intestinal microbiota was significantly decreased in persons with AD (all <i>p</i> < 0.05)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37577447> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37606895_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37606895_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "At least 12 cohort studies, four of which also included controls documented the occurrence of post-COVID-19 DGBI, particularly IBS following COVID-19." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37606895> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37607587_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37607587_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Dysbiosis (a dysfunctional microbiome) drives increased intestinal permeability and inflammation that can negatively affect the brain via the gut-brain axis." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37607587> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37627638_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37627638_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Essential oils sourced from herbs commonly used in the Mediterranean diet have demonstrated advantageous attributes as nutraceuticals and prebiotics within a model of severe cardiometabolic disorder." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37627638> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37627638_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37627638_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We observed a substantial increase in the relative abundance of the <i>Lactobacillus</i> genus in the gut microbiota, accompanied by higher levels of short-chain fatty acids and a reduction in trimethylamine N-oxide levels and protein oxidation in the plasma." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37627638> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37655441_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37655441_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "<i>Prevotella copri</i> is an abundant member of the human gastrointestinal microbiome, whose relative abundance has curiously been associated with positive and negative impacts on diseases, such as Parkinson's disease and rheumatoid arthritis." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37655441> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37657622_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37657622_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Although the association between gut microbiota and the pathogenesis of major depressive disorder (MDD) has been well studied, it is unclear whether gut microbiota affects cognitive function in patients with MDD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37657622> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37657622_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37657622_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Compared with HCs, two strains (bin_32 and bin_55) were significantly increased, and one strain (bin_31) was significantly decreased in patients with MDD based on the strain-level meta-analysis." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37657622> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37676767_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37676767_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Fiber deprivation and microbiome-borne curli shift gut bacterial populations and accelerate disease in a mouse model of Parkinson's disease." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37676767> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37676767_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37676767_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Diet-driven gut dysbiosis and reduced barrier function may increase exposure of enteric neurons to toxins." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37676767> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37764088_11> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37764088_11" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Although we have not established a direct link between GM and CC risk, our findings indicate that GM of preschoolers is closely associated with emotional processing and that EERrisk children have more inflammation-related bacteria." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37764088> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37834373_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37834373_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The gut microbiome plays a pivotal role in maintaining human health, with numerous studies demonstrating that alterations in microbial compositions can significantly affect the development and progression of various immune-mediated diseases affecting both the digestive tract and the central nervous system (CNS)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37834373> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37834373_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37834373_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The role of the gut microbiota in the pathogenesis of neurodegenerative diseases has gained increasing attention in recent years, and evidence suggests that gut dysbiosis may contribute to disease development and progression." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37834373> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37834373_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37834373_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Clinical studies have shown alterations in the composition of the gut microbiota in multiple sclerosis patients, with a decrease in beneficial bacteria and an increase in pro-inflammatory bacteria." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37834373> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37834373_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37834373_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Microbiota-gut-brain communication can impact neurodegenerative diseases through various mechanisms, including the regulation of immune function, the production of microbial metabolites, as well as modulation of host-derived soluble factors." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37834373> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37834373_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37834373_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This review describes the current literature on the gut-brain axis and highlights novel communication systems that allow cross-talk between the gut microbiota and the host that might influence the pathogenesis of neuroinflammation and neurodegeneration." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37834373> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37841274_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37841274_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Melanin: a unifying theory of disease as exemplified by Parkinson's, Alzheimer's, and Lewy body dementia." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37841274> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37841274_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37841274_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Our theory that energy retained in melanin fuels cells in an inverse relationship with ATP is supported by studies showing alterations in ATP production in relationship to melanin levels in melanomas, vitiligo, and healthy cells." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37841274> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37849234_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37849234_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Alzheimer's disease is a complex neurodegenerative disorder leading to a decline in cognitive function and mental health." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37849234> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37849234_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37849234_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Our findings reveal for the first time, that Alzheimer's symptoms can be transferred to a healthy young organism via the gut microbiota, confirming a causal role of gut microbiota in Alzheimer's disease, and highlight hippocampal neurogenesis as a converging central cellular process regulating systemic circulatory and gut-mediated factors in Alzheimer's." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37849234> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37849234_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37849234_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Recent research has positioned the gut microbiota as an important susceptibility factor in Alzheimer's disease by showing specific alterations in the gut microbiome composition of Alzheimer's patients and in rodent models." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37849234> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37849234_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37849234_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "However, it is unknown whether gut microbiota alterations are causal in the manifestation of Alzheimer's symptoms." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37849234> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37881577_11> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37881577_11" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "RSDS mice also showed a specific increase in intestinal expression of claudin-2, a tight junction protein, and epinephrine, a stress-induced neurotransmitter." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37881577> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37881577_12> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37881577_12" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Treating intestinal epithelial cells or 3-dimensional cultured crypts with norepinephrine or intestinal luminal contents (fecal contents) upregulated claudin-2 expression and inhibited transepithelial electrical resistance." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37881577> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37881577_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37881577_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We used a mouse model of repeated social defeat stress (RSDS), a preclinical model of PTSD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37881577> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37900921_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37900921_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "However, we found no data on the presence or quantity of 4EP and/or 4EPS in human brains, irrespective of neurological status, likely due to challenges sampling this organ." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37900921> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37927130_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37927130_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Our previous study showed that chronic consumption of <i>Lactobacillus reuteri</i> ATG-F4 (F4) induced neurometabolic alterations in healthy mice." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37927130> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37960197_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37960197_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Multivariable MR (MVMR) was employed to ascertain the causal independence between gut microbiota and the metabolites linked to OSA." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37960197> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37960197_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37960197_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Additionally, Cochran's Q test, the MR Egger intercept test and the MR Steiger test were used for the sensitivity analyses." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37960197> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37960197_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37960197_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Among the 83 metabolites evaluated, 3-dehydrocarnitine, epiandrosterone sulfate, and leucine were determined to be potential independent risk factors associated with OSA." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37960197> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37978477_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37978477_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "By exploring the intricate relationship between the gut and the brain, with the goal of offering fresh perspectives and valuable insights into the potential contribution of intestinal microbial and metabolites dysbiosis to the etiology of schizophrenia." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37978477> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37995075_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37995075_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Depression is one of the complications in patients with polycystic ovary syndrome (PCOS) that leads to considerable mental health." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37995075> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37995075_12> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37995075_12" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Our multi-omics data indicate shifts in the gut microbiome and host gene regulation in PCOS patients with depression, which is of possible etiological and diagnostic importance." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37995075> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37995075_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37995075_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "However, whether microbiota influences depression development in PCOS patients is still uncharacterized." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37995075> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37995075_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37995075_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Gut microbiota assessment revealed distinct patterns in the relative abundance in the PCOS-DP compared to HC, MDD, and PCOS groups." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37995075> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37995075_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37995075_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "RNA-seq profiling identified that 35 and 37 genes were significantly elevated and downregulated in the PCOS-DP, respectively." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37995075> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37995475_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37995475_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This indicates that the divergence in beta diversity in the narcolepsy type 1 and idiopathic hypersomnia groups did not arise due to sleep disturbances." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37995475> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37995475_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37995475_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We did not observe any changes in the alpha diversity of the gut microbiota among patient groups and healthy controls." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37995475> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37995475_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37995475_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We observed changes in beta diversity in accordance with Jaccard dissimilarities between the control group and groups of patients suffering from narcolepsy type 1 and idiopathic hypersomnia." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37995475> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/38010793_11> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_38010793_11" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Among the altered metabolites, ten metabolites derived from microbiota (<i>Turicibacter</i>, <i>Coprococcus 1</i>, Eggerthellaceae, and <i>Clostridium sp. BR31</i>) were screened out" ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/38010793> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/38010793_14> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_38010793_14" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Collectively, our research provides insights into the relationship between diet, the gut microbiota, and GI symptoms in children with ASD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/38010793> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/38011787_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_38011787_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This study sheds light on the potential therapeutic role of CPT in managing depressive disorders, offering a comprehensive understanding of its impact on behavior, inflammation, gut microbiota, and molecular pathways." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/38011787> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/38045924_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_38045924_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In this narrative review, we summarize the mechanisms underlying the microbiota-gut-brain axis involvement in epilepsy, discuss the impact of antiepileptic drugs on the gut microbiome, and then the impact of a particular dietary pattern, the ketogenic diet, on the microbiota-gut-brain axis in epileptic patients." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/38045924> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/38068763_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_38068763_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "(2) Methods: We examined whether the use of probiotics and improved eating habits can improve the mental health of people who suffered from mood disorders after bariatric surgery." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/38068763> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/38123016_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_38123016_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This review highlights that RNA sequencing, metabolomics, and transcriptomics data are needed to understand how microbial modulators can influence ASD pathophysiology." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/38123016> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/38132705_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
