<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/23981537_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_23981537_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The first wave of danger signals consists of the release of metabolic intermediates like ATP and ADP, Krebs cycle intermediates, oxygen, and reactive oxygen species (ROS), and is sustained by purinergic signaling." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/23981537> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/25034760_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_25034760_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Co-morbid GI inflammation accompanies humoral immunity to food antigens, occurs early during the course of schizophrenia and appears to be independent from antipsychotic-generated motility effects." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/25034760> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/25231862_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_25231862_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We identify NAS-altered microbial metabolic pathways that are linked to host susceptibility to metabolic disease, and demonstrate similar NAS-induced dysbiosis and glucose intolerance in healthy human subjects." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/25231862> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/26129950_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_26129950_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In the current study, antibiotics were used to disturb the gut microbiota of both rats fed a high-cholesterol diet and rats fed a normal diet (controls)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/26129950> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/26129950_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_26129950_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This may have been due to an increase in intestinal permeability and plasma lipopolysaccharide (LPS), which lead to an increase in LPS absorption and activation of TLR4 signaling, resulting in the synthesis of pro-inflammatory cytokines and chemokines in liver tissues." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/26129950> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/26190966_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_26190966_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Obesity is associated with a high prevalence of mood disorders and cognitive dysfunctions in addition to being a significant risk factor for important health complications such as cardiovascular diseases and type 2 diabetes." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/26190966> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/27566465_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_27566465_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Germ-free animals, antibiotics, probiotics intervention and diet can induce alterations of gut microbiota and gut physiology and also host cognitive behavior, increasing or decreasing risks of AD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/27566465> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28073356_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28073356_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Factors supporting this hypothesis are: 1) research focusing on intelligence and school performance in school-aged children has shown helminth infections to be associated with cognitive impairment, 2) disturbances in gut microbiota have been shown to be associated with important cognitive developmental effects, and 3) helminth infections have been shown to alter the gut microbiota structure." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28073356> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28399458_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28399458_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The role of maternal anxiety and depressive disorders prior to and during pregnancy and perinatal psychopathological symptoms for early infant diseases and drug administration." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/28399458> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28399458_11> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28399458_11" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Moreover, the association between maternal anxiety and depressive disorders and infant gastrointestinal complaints may be explained by an anxious misinterpretation of 'normal' infant signals or a transmission of adverse gut microbiota, respectively." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28399458> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28399458_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28399458_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "To prospectively investigate associations of anxiety and depressive disorders prior to and during pregnancy as well as perinatal distress with infants' inflammatory diseases, gastrointestinal complaints and corresponding drug administration." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28399458> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28556833_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28556833_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Furthermore, treatment with MR16-1 could significantly normalize alterations in the expression of synaptic proteins (postsynaptic density protein 95 and α-amino-3-hydroxy-5-methyl-4-isoxazolepropionic acid receptor 1) and dendritic spine density in the brain regions of susceptible mice." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28556833> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28629758_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28629758_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Although plasma and brain cytokines were not significantly altered in socially defeated mice, changes in the mRNA expression of interleukin (IL)-1β and IL-6 within the prefrontal cortex were associated with elevated abundance of Flavobacterium spp." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28629758> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28816544_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28816544_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Expert opinion: Mounting evidence implicates microglia, polyunsaturated fatty acids (PUFAs), glucocorticoids and gut microbiota in both inflammation and depression." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28816544> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28843021_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28843021_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Microbiota of flash-frozen stool and nasal wash samples from 76 PD patients, 21 idiopathic rapid eye movement sleep behavior disorder patients, and 78 healthy controls were assessed by 16S and 18S ribosomal RNA amplicon sequencing." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28843021> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/28852308_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_28852308_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Here, we review the evidence supporting a role of the gut microbiota in neuropsychiatric disorders and the state of the art regarding the mechanisms underlying its contribution to mental illness and health." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/28852308> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/29249803_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_29249803_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "At the phylum level, CSDS-susceptible mice showed alterations in the levels of Tenericutes and Actinobacteria; however, neither ketamine enantiomers influenced these alterations." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/29249803> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/29352709_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_29352709_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In this study, we first compared the difference of gut microbiota between schizophrenia patients and healthy controls by 16S rRNA sequencing." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/29352709> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30072879_14> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30072879_14" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "MPTP reduced striatal TH levels in WT and KO mice but these effects were only pronounced in males." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30072879> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30072879_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30072879_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Two-week sub-chronic MPTP increased activity of female and male wild-type (WT) and mGlu8 knockout (KO) mice in the open field." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30072879> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30394313_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30394313_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "MEs identified in ASD children with GI problems were significantly more diverse than those in TD children." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30394313> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30459574_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30459574_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Probiotics attenuated CMS-induced anxiety- and depressive-like behaviors, significantly increased <i>Lactobacillus</i> abundance, and reversed the CMS-induced immune changes in the hippocampus." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30459574> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30518033_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30518033_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Four different breeds of 5-week-old mice were used in this experiment: Balb/c, Orient C57BL/6N, Taconic C57BL/6N, and Taconic C57BL/6J." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30518033> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30528936_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30528936_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Ketamine (10 mg/kg) significantly attenuated the increased immobility time in forced swimming test (FST), which was associated with the improvements in α-diversity, consisting of Shannon, Simpson and Chao 1 indices." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30528936> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30584306_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30584306_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Several studies have shown that patients with depression were also accompanied with gut microbiota disorder, in which Firmicutes are related to the protective function of intestinal barrier." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30584306> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30701194_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30701194_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "At the validation stage, differential metabolites were tested using LC-MS with an additional 49 and 11 children in the ASD and TD groups, respectively." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30701194> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30707176_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30707176_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Fecal samples from 20 VVS children and 20 matched controls were collected, and the microbiota were analyzed by 16S rRNA gene sequencing." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30707176> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/30828318_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_30828318_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "(ii) What components of the gut microbiota and their function, including as it relates to mental health, are critical and how do they differ between agile, fit hunter gatherers and obese westerners or Danes described as the happiest people on the planet?" ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/30828318> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31053995_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31053995_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The results indicate that this panel of NAPEs is able to distinguish female PD patients from the corresponding healthy controls." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31053995> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31083360_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31083360_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "<i>Methods</i>: Using the keywords (prebiotics OR probiotics OR microbiota OR gut) AND (autism OR social OR ASD), a systematic literature search was conducted on PubMed, EMBASE, Medline, Clinicaltrials.gov and Google Scholar databases." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31083360> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31132457_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31132457_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Three sample clusters (Bifidobacterium/Enterobacteriaceae, Bacteroides, V. Dispar) based on GMC were identified, of which Bifidobacterium/Enterobacteriaceae-cluster presented with higher scores on the IBQ-R main dimension regulation and its subscale duration of orienting compared to Bacteroides-cluster." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31132457> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31154909_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31154909_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Some of the claimed negative health outcomes associated with milk consumption, such as cardiovascular diseases and type 1 diabetes may be attributed to an opioid peptide, beta-casomorphin-7 (BCM-7), derived from A1 beta-casein." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31154909> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31179435_12> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31179435_12" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In the studies that used treatment as usual plus interventions regulating intestinal flora (IRIF) as interventions (five studies), only non-probiotic ways were effective (two studies), which means 40% of studies were effective; in the studies that used IRIF alone (16 studies, 11 studies used probiotic ways and 5 studies used non-probiotic ways), 56% of studies could improve anxiety symptoms, and 80% of studies that conducted the non-probiotic interventions were effective, while 45% of studies that used probiotic supplementations had positive effects on anxiety symptoms." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31179435> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31248424_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31248424_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Here, we evaluate gut microbiota alterations and host cytokine responses in a population of Taiwanese patients with PD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31248424> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31248424_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31248424_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Fecal microbiota communities from 80 patients with PD and 77 age and gender-matched controls were assessed by sequencing the V3-V4 region of the 16S ribosomal RNA gene." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31248424> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31488882_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31488882_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Sodium oligomannate therapeutically remodels gut microbiota and suppresses gut bacterial amino acids-shaped neuroinflammation to inhibit Alzheimer's disease progression." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/31488882> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31488882_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31488882_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Importantly, the elevation of phenylalanine and isoleucine concentrations and the increase of Th1 cell frequency in the blood were also observed in two small independent cohorts of patients with mild cognitive impairment (MCI) due to AD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31488882> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31488882_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31488882_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Together, our findings highlight the role of gut dysbiosis-promoted neuroinflammation in AD progression and suggest a novel strategy for AD therapy by remodelling the gut microbiota." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31488882> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31498131_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31498131_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Gut microbiota have been studied in relation to the pathophysiology of Parkinson's disease (PD) due to the early gastrointestinal symptomatology and presence of alpha-synuclein pathology in the enteric nervous system, hypothesized to ascend via the vagal nerve to the central nervous system." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31498131> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31498131_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31498131_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Furthermore, expansion of the current dataset with atypical parkinsonism cohorts, prodromal and treatment-naïve de novo PD subjects, measurements of fecal microbial concentrations and multi-omics assessments are required to provide clinically relevant biomarkers and reveal therapeutic targets within the gut microbiome of PD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31498131> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31530799_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31530799_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The compositions of gut microbiota and short-chain fatty acids were assessed in fecal samples from control rats, non-LH (resilient) rats, and LH (susceptible) rats." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31530799> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31530799_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31530799_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "At the genus level, the numbers of Lactobacillus, Clostridium cluster III, and Anaerofustis in susceptible rats were significantly higher than in control and resilient rats." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31530799> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31530799_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31530799_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Levels of acetic acid and propionic acid in the feces of susceptible rats were lower than in those of control and resilient rats; however, the levels of lactic acid in the susceptible rats were higher than those of control and resilient rats." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31530799> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31596658_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31596658_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "<b><i>Results</i>:</b> Recent work by our research group has demonstrated that PBM (red and NIR light) delivered to the abdomen in mice, can alter the gut microbiome in a potentially beneficial way." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31596658> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31685046_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31685046_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Four Kyoto Encyclopedia of Genes and Genomes (KEGG) orthologies (KOs) (K01817, K11358, K01626, K01667) abundances in the MiTBamp were significantly lower in the MDD group." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31685046> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31726457_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31726457_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The microbiota-gut-brain axis is a dynamic matrix of tissues and organs including the gastrointestinal (GI) microbiota, immune cells, gut tissue, glands, the autonomic nervous system (ANS), and the brain that communicate in a complex multidirectional manner through a number of anatomically and physiologically distinct systems." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31726457> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31917834_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31917834_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Also, pubertal neuroinflammatory insults can alter neurodevelopment, impact brain functioning in an enduring manner, and contribute to neurological disorders related to brain aging, such as Alzheimer's disease, Parkinson's disease, and depression." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31917834> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31952911_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31952911_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We aimed to systematically review studies of alterations in gut microbiota of patients suffering from psychotic disorders, bipolar disorder or depression compared to healthy controls." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31952911> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/31952911_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_31952911_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Primary outcome was to compare the gut microbiota of patients suffering from psychotic disorders, bipolar disorder or depression with healthy controls." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/31952911> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32041265_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32041265_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The impact of the gut microbiome is being increasingly appreciated in health and in various chronic diseases, among them neurodegenerative disorders such as Parkinson's disease (PD)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32041265> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32056910_12> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32056910_12" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Conclusions Well-designed case-control and longitudinal studies are required to disentangle whether the gut microbiota is predicted as a continuum of gastrointestinal and anxiety/depression symptom severity, or whether reported dysbiosis is unique to IBS and anxiety/depression comorbidity." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32056910> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32056910_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32056910_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Most studies investigated the gut microbiota and anxiety/depression symptoms in IBS cohorts." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32056910> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32379622_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32379622_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "CSDS did not produce an anhedonia-like phenotype in the betaine-treated mice, but did induce an anhedonia-like phenotype in water-treated mice." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32379622> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32431588_11> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32431588_11" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Collectively, our findings provide the basis for future developments of probiotic, prebiotic, or synbiotic approaches for modulating the onset and/or progression of α-synucleinopathies." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32431588> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32431588_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32431588_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Here we investigate whether 3-HBA, 4-hydroxybenzoic acid (4-HBA), 3,4-diHBA, or 3-HPPA interfere with α-syn spreading in a cell-based system." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32431588> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32431588_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32431588_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We demonstrated that 3-HPPA, 3,4-diHBA, 3-HBA, and 4-HBA significantly attenuated intracellular α-syn seeding aggregation." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32431588> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32518376_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32518376_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "A key role of the subdiaphragmatic vagus nerve in the depression-like phenotype and abnormal composition of gut microbiota in mice after lipopolysaccharide administration." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/32518376> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32572814_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32572814_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Parkinson's disease (PD), a progressive neurodegenerative disorder, is associated with the destruction of dopamine neurons in the substantia nigra (SN) and the formation of Lewy bodies in basal ganglia." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32572814> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32739746_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32739746_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In mice, bacterial members of the gut microbiota can influence the host gut-brain axis, affecting anxiety-like behavior and the hypothalamus-pituitary-adrenal (HPA) axis which produces the stress hormone corticosterone (CORT)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32739746> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32816830_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32816830_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This diet reduces the intake of fermentable fibres, leading to changes of the gut microbiota and insufficient fermentation in the large bowel, resulting in reduced production of short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs), such as butyrate, which has unfavourable implications for gut health, sleep and mental health." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32816830> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32819434_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32819434_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The gut microbiota regulates autism-like behavior by mediating vitamin B<sub>6</sub> homeostasis in EphB6-deficient mice." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/32819434> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32819434_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32819434_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "At the metabolic level, the disturbed gut microbiota in EphB6-deficient mice led to vitamin B<sub>6</sub> and dopamine defects." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32819434> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32979562_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32979562_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Shotgun metagenomics reveals both taxonomic and tryptophan pathway differences of gut microbiota in bipolar disorder with current major depressive episode patients." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/32979562> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32979562_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32979562_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We performed shotgun metagenomics sequencing (SMS) of faecal samples from 25 BPD patients and 28 healthy controls (HCs)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32979562> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32979562_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32979562_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Compared to HCs, the phylum Bacteroidetes abundance was significantly reduced, whereas that of the Actinobacteria and Firmicutes were significantly increased in BPD patients." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32979562> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/32999308_11> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_32999308_11" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Further, inflammatory genes related to PD were augmented in the midbrain of DJ-1<sup>-/-</sup> mice." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/32999308> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33067915_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33067915_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We examined 116 children with ASD and 860 without ASD and found that flu in second trimester was associated with increased ASD, but only among women who did not take an antibiotic during pregnancy." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33067915> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33076930_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33076930_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We detected 3-(3,4-dihydroxyphenyl)propionic acid in fecal samples of Parkinson's disease patients on levodopa medication and found that this metabolite is actively produced by the gut microbiota in those stool samples." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33076930> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33105830_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33105830_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Disturbance to the gut microbiota leads to immune dysfunction both locally and at distant sites, which causes inflammatory conditions not only in the intestine but also in the other organs such as lungs and brain, and may induce a disease state." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33105830> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33144709_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33144709_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "These include modulation of pathways involved in inflammation, oxidative stress, epigenetics, mitochondrial dysfunction, the gut microbiota, tryptophan-kynurenine metabolism, the HPA axis, neurogenesis and BDNF, epigenetics, and obesity." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33144709> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33212907_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33212907_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "All participants with HbA1c 40-50 mmol/mol commenced intermittent fasting (2 days per week of calorie restriction to 600-650 kcal/day) and were randomized 1:1 to either daily probiotic (<i>Lacticaseibacillus rhamnosus</i> HN001) or placebo for 12 weeks." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33212907> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33301807_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33301807_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In this review, the complications following SCI, including intestinal dysfunction, anxiety and depression, metabolic disorders, and neuropathic pain, are directly or indirectly related to gut dysbiosis, which may be mediated by \"gut-brain\" interactions." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33301807> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33406628_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33406628_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We investigated the changes in the functional microbiota in the appendix of PD patients relative to controls (<i>n</i> = 12 PD, 16 C) by metatranscriptomic analysis." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33406628> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33422110_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33422110_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Recent work has established that Parkinson's disease (PD) patients have an altered gut microbiome, along with signs of intestinal inflammation." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33422110> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33467657_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33467657_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We review currently available preclinical and clinical evidence and summarise possible underlying neurobiological mechanisms by which maternal overnutrition may perturb offspring cognitive function, affective state and psychosocial behaviour, with a focus on (1) neuroinflammation; (2) disrupted neuronal circuities and connectivity; and (3) dysregulated brain hormones." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33467657> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33511258_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33511258_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Probiotic consumption relieved human stress and anxiety symptoms possibly via modulating the neuroactive potential of the gut microbiota." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/33511258> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33511258_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33511258_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Furthermore, the 12-week probiotic supplementation enhanced the diversity of neurotransmitter-synthesizing/consuming SGBs and the levels of some predicted microbial neuroactive metabolites (e.g., short-chain fatty acids, gamma-aminobutyric acid, arachidonic acid, and sphingomyelin)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33511258> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33514545_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33514545_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "It connects microphysiological systems (MPSs) of the primary human gut and liver with a human induced pluripotent stem cell-derived cerebral MPS in a systemically circulated common culture medium containing CD4<sup>+</sup> regulatory T and T helper 17 cells." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33514545> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33664475_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33664475_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Compared to control mice, WT offspring deprived of 6'SL during lactation exhibited consistent alterations in all cognitive functions addressed, hippocampal electrophysiology, and in pathways regulating the serotonergic system (identified through gut microbiota and plasma metabolomics)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33664475> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33677218_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33677218_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Fecal microbiota transplantation ameliorates stress-induced depression-like behaviors associated with the inhibition of glial and NLRP3 inflammasome in rat brain." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/33677218> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33677218_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33677218_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Moreover, fecal microbiota transplantation administration suppressed the activation of Iba1 positive microglia cells and GFAP positive astrocytes cells and reduced the expression of NLRP3, ASC, Caspase-1, and IL-1β pathway in the prefrontal cortex and hippocampus." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33677218> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33692356_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33692356_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This dysbiosis might result in a pro-inflammatory status which could be linked to the recurrent gastrointestinal symptoms affecting PD patients." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33692356> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33713734_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33713734_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Background Affective disorders (AD) have been associated with a higher prevalence of the gut Flavonifractor genus and a lower abundance of the gut Christensenellaceae family." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33713734> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33713734_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33713734_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Conclusion Compared with findings in healthy controls, AD was associated with a significantly lower CLR abundance of the health-linked Christensenellaceae and a significantly higher prevalence of Flavonifractor; findings that are associated with enhanced oxidative stress and systemic low-grade inflammation." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33713734> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33713734_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33713734_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Objective and methods By pooling two independent study samples of patients with AD (n = 176), their unaffected first-degree relatives (n = 70) and healthy controls (n = 101) we aimed to replicate and extend our prior findings of differential Flavonifractor prevalence and Christensenellaceae abundance when comparing patients with AD and healthy controls." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33713734> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33722869_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33722869_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The Bugs and Brains Study aims to recruit 160 females to the primary component: (1) 40 controls; (2) 40 participants with a depressive/anxiety disorder, but no IBS; (3) 40 participants with IBS, but no depressive/anxiety disorder and (4) 40 participants with both depressive/anxiety disorder and IBS." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33722869> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33807447_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33807447_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Within a 4-week, monocentric, randomized, controlled trial with a parallel group design (vegan (VD) vs. meat-rich (MD)) with 53 healthy, omnivore, normal-weight participants (62% female, mean 31 years of age), fecal samples were collected at the beginning and at the end of the trial and were analyzed using 16S rRNA gene amplicon sequencing (Clinical Trial register: DRKS00011963)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33807447> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33860090_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33860090_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Several preclinical and clinical studies have demonstrated disrupted intestinal permeability, intestinal inflammation, altered gut microbiome, and reduced fecal short-chain fatty acids in PD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33860090> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33936013_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33936013_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Emerging evidence has revealed the presence of the glutamate decarboxylase (GAD)-encoding gene, a key enzyme to produce GABA, in the prominent human intestinal genus <i>Bacteroides</i>." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33936013> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33936013_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33936013_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We identified glutamate and glutamine as precursors of GABA production, showed that the production is regulated by pH, and that the GAD-system acts as a protective mechanism against acid stress in <i>Bacteroides</i>, mitigating cell death and preserving metabolic activity." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33936013> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33963281_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33963281_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Sleep deprivation (SD) is increasingly common in modern society, which can lead to the dysregulation of inflammatory responses and cognitive impairment, but the mechanisms remain unclear." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33963281> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33963281_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33963281_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Transplantation of the \"SD microbiota\" into GF mice activated the Toll-like receptor 4/nuclear factor-κB signaling pathway and impaired cognitive function in the recipient mice." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33963281> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33963281_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33963281_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Mice that harbored \"SD microbiota\" also exhibited increases in neuroinflammation and microglial activity in the hippocampus and medial prefrontal cortex." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33963281> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33967849_11> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33967849_11" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "<b>Conclusion:</b> There is limited but promising evidence about the effectiveness of probiotics during pregnancy to reduce anxiety symptoms and reduce the proportion of women scoring ABOVE a cut-off depression score." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33967849> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33967849_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33967849_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This systematic review evaluated the effectiveness of prebiotics, probiotics, and synbiotics supplementation during pregnancy to reduce the risk of maternal mental health problems in the perinatal period." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33967849> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/33968794_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_33968794_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Intestinal dysbiosis is likely involved in the pathogenesis of Parkinson's disease through mechanisms that include barrier destruction, inflammation and oxidative stress, decreased dopamine production, and molecular mimicry." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/33968794> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34032650_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34032650_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "EU-funded guidelines recommend that patients with depression or vulnerability to depression should be encouraged to enhance a plant-based diet with a high content of grains/fibres, fermented foods, and fish." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34032650> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34092293_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34092293_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Studies on blood enrichment and anti-tumor effects of combined Danggui Buxue Decoction (DBD), Fe and rhEPO based on CCRA and gut microbiota modulation were conducted in this paper." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34092293> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34092293_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34092293_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The sequencing results of gut microbiota showed that compared to P group, the relative abundances of Lachnospiraceae and opportunistic pathogen (Odoribacter) in ED and EDF groups were decreased." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34092293> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34147969_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34147969_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Ingestion of Faecalibaculum rodentium causes depression-like phenotypes in resilient Ephx2 knock-out mice: A role of brain-gut-microbiota axis via the subdiaphragmatic vagus nerve." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/34147969> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34147969_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34147969_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The 16S ribosome RNA analysis showed that Faecalibaculum rodentium (F. rodentium) may be responsible for the observed anhedonia-like behavior following FMT from CSDS-susceptible mice." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34147969> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34174901_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34174901_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Beyond the lesion site: minocycline augments inflammation and anxiety-like behavior following SCI in rats through action on the gut microbiota." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/34174901> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34174901_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34174901_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Here, we sought to determine minocycline's effect on spinal cord injury-induced changes in the microbiota-immune axis using a cervical contusion injury in female Lewis rats." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34174901> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34290352_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34290352_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We recruited 30 MDD patients (MDD group) and 30 healthy controls (control group)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34290352> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34311029_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34311029_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Lipid analyses and lipidomic studies reveal changes in specific lipid types with aging and AD, which can identify potential lipid-based nutraceuticals to restore the brain to a healthy lipid phenotype." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34311029> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34311029_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34311029_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In this review, we briefly discuss the role of lipids in the brain, the changing lipid profile in AD, current research on lipid-based nutraceuticals and their therapeutic potential to combat cognitive impairment." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34311029> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34393849_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34393849_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We recruited 126 participants and divided them into three groups according to the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, Fifth Edition, criteria-acute group (patients with acute schizophrenia), remission group (patients with schizophrenia in remission), and control group (healthy controls)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34393849> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34399524_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34399524_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "A high AGE-diet led to an increase of AGEs in plasma, kidney, and liver and to more inflammation and modification of the gut microbiota." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34399524> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34408160_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34408160_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Genetic studies have shown that overexpression of alpha-synuclein, a key pathological protein in Parkinson's disease (PD), can cause familial PD and variants at alpha-synuclein locus confer risk of idiopathic PD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34408160> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34408160_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34408160_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Using two large datasets, we found evidence that the overabundance of opportunistic pathogens in PD gut is influenced by the host genotype at the alpha-synuclein locus, and that the variants responsible modulate alpha-synuclein expression." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34408160> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34437440_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34437440_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In this study, we recruited more than 300 biopsy specimens from people undergoing colonoscopy, and we analyzed to determine whether a correlation exists between the presence of bacterial genes coding for toxins possibly involved in CRC onset and progression and the different stages of CRC." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34437440> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34437440_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34437440_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Toxins from <i>Escherichia coli</i> as a whole have a higher incidence rate in adenocarcinoma patients compared to controls, whereas <i>Bacteroides fragilis</i> toxin does not seem to be associated with pre-cancerous nor with cancerous lesions." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34437440> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34444820_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34444820_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The NVP-1704 group had a more significant reduction in depressive symptoms at four and eight weeks of treatment, and anxiety symptoms at four weeks compared to the placebo group." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34444820> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34480631_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34480631_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Microglial depletion and abnormalities in gut microbiota composition and short-chain fatty acids in mice after repeated administration of colony stimulating factor 1 receptor inhibitor PLX5622." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/34480631> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34520319_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34520319_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Further, impaired sleep and circadian patterns are common symptoms of AD, while sleep and circadian rhythm disruption (SCRD) is associated with greater β-amyloid (Aβ) burden and AD risk, sometimes years before the clinical onset of AD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34520319> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34589800_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34589800_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Accumulating evidence have positioned inflammatory signaling pathways as crucial routes by which microbes inhabiting the gastrointestinal tract (the gut microbiota) communicate with the host brain to influence behavior, with impacts on mental illnesses." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34589800> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34758889_12> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34758889_12" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We exploit these findings for SCFA receptor knockout mice and oral SCFA supplementation that verified SCFA playing a critical role linking the altered gut microbiota and cognitive impairment." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34758889> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34758889_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34758889_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "A hippocampal proteomic analysis further identified a deficit of CaMKIId and its associated synaptic proteins (including GAP43 and SV2C) in the FD mice, along with neuroinflammation and microglial engulfment of synapses." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34758889> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34836918_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34836918_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Taken together, our results demonstrate that chronic exposure to dietary BMAA can trigger a chain of events that recapitulate the evolution of the PD pathology from the gut to the brain, which is consistent with 'gut-first' PD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34836918> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34870091_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34870091_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We will perform a systematic review and meta-analysis to identify, evaluate and if possible, combine the published literature on compositional alterations in the oral and gut microbiota in patients with psychosis or schizophrenia compared with healthy controls." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34870091> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34961418_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34961418_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The abundance of firmicutes and coliform were significantly lower and the abundance of bacteroides significantly higher in patients who received berberine compared to placebo after 12 weeks of treatment ([Formula: see text]< 0.05)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34961418> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34970638_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34970638_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "CUMS and dexamethasone induce depression-like phenotypes in mice by differentially altering gut microbiota and triggering macroglia activation." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/34970638> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/34970638_11> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_34970638_11" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Prevotellaceae and Desulfovibrio were enriched, whereas Bacilli were decreased in the faeces of mice in the CUMS group." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/34970638> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35207632_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35207632_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We propose that by targeting the intestinal barrier, ENS, and/or the gut microbiome, may prove successful in alleviating PD-related GI symptoms, and discuss emerging therapies and potential drugs that could be repurposed to target these areas." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35207632> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35281490_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35281490_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Dysbiosis is also linked to psychiatric and gastrointestinal complications - comorbidities often associated with the prodromal phase of Parkinson's disease (PD) and Alzheimer's disease (AD)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35281490> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35326429_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35326429_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Gut bacteria responsible for increased H<sub>2</sub>S production, especially the mucus-associated species of the bacterial genera belonging to the Desulfovibrionaceae and Enterobacteriaceae families, are likely play a role in the pathogenesis of Parkinson's disease." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35326429> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35432226_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35432226_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Based on the etiology of each proposed progression, individuals with the body-first progression may exhibit altered gut microbiomes, i.e., where short-chain fatty acid producing bacteria are reduced, while the brain-first progression may not." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35432226> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35571084_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35571084_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Targeting bacterial amyloid production may serve as a novel therapeutic strategy for treating NDs, and several compounds, such as epigallocatechin-3-gallate (EGCG), were shown to suppress neurodegeneration at least partly by inhibiting curli production." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35571084> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35674870_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35674870_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Neuroinflammation plays a significant role in Parkinson's disease (PD) etiology along with mitochondrial dysfunction and impaired proteostasis." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35674870> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/35914559_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_35914559_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "To assess this, we collected fecal samples from adult rats treated with 200 mg/kg TCE over 6 weeks via oral gavage - the dose that produced nigrostriatal neurodegeneration - and analyzed the gut microbiome via whole genome shotgun sequencing." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/35914559> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36191806_11> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36191806_11" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "These data suggest that Chrna7 KO mice produce depression-like behaviors and reduced expression of synaptic proteins in the mPFC through gut-microbiota-brain axis via subdiaphragmatic vagus nerve." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36191806> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36216056_13> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36216056_13" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Fecal microbiome transplantation from PM group mice reproduced excitability and anxiety symptoms." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36216056> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36216056_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36216056_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Therefore, a multi-omics animal experiment was conducted to verify how urban PM induces SCZ-like behavior and altered gut microbiota and metabolic pathways." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36216056> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36216056_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36216056_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Besides, fecal microbiome of PM group and control group were transplanted into \"pseudo-sterile\" mice, then behavioral tests were conducted." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36216056> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36346385_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36346385_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Parkinson's disease (PD) is a movement disorder characterized by neuroinflammation, α-synuclein pathology, and neurodegeneration." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36346385> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36411639_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36411639_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Microbes present in the human gut can affect brain function by the release of neuroactive metabolites such as neurotransmitters, hormones, and other compounds." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36411639> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36462169_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36462169_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Gut microbiota alterations have been reported in severe mental illness (SMI) but fewer studies have probed for signs of gut barrier disruption and inflammation." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36462169> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36493975_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36493975_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Key role of the gut-microbiota-brain axis via the subdiaphragmatic vagus nerve in demyelination of the cuprizone-treated mouse brain." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/36493975> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36517709_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36517709_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "PHP significantly prevented increases in serum total cholesterol, triglycerides and low-density lipoprotein cholesterol, and alleviated damage to liver cells induced by a high-fat diet M. auratus, in a dose-dependent manner." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36517709> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36550591_14> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36550591_14" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "XPJYF elevated 2-DG uptake, ATP, glucose-1-phosphate, and brain-derived neurotrophic factor (BDNF), and inhibited cytokines and oxidative stress in LPS-induced astrocyte." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36550591> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36651663_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36651663_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "This study investigated fecal microbial features associated with mental health outcomes (symptoms of anxiety, depression, or posttraumatic stress disorder (PTSD)) in a Spanish cohort in the aftermath of the COVID-19 pandemic." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36651663> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36698474_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36698474_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Then, following the rise of the ratios of meat to pulses, eggs to pulses, and pork to pulses, the usage of fertilizers, the farming density of pigs, and the burdens of the above disease except diabetes mellitus were also ever-increasing." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36698474> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36699448_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36699448_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "A species of the <i>Romboutsia</i> genus was co-associated with the species of <i>Ruminococcus gnavus</i> in an internetwork through four genes: <i>METTL8</i>, <i>ITGB2</i>, <i>OTULIN</i>, and <i>PROSER3</i>, with a strict threshold (<i>p</i> < 5 × 10<sup>-4</sup>)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36699448> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36738999_13> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36738999_13" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Further, Pearson correlation analysis showed that Akkermansia_muciniphila was significantly negatively correlated with the concentration of MCP-1, IL-17A in serum and 5-HT in hippocampus." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36738999> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36794003_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36794003_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The glucose homeostasis of participants with T2DM was improved by the high-fiber diet, and the serum metabolome, systemic inflammation and psychiatric comorbidities were also altered." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36794003> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36804535_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "A single administration of arketamine (10 mg/kg) ameliorated anhedonia-like behavior and decreased femoral neck cortical (and total) BMD in CSDS susceptible mice." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36804535> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36804535_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "These data suggest that, in addition to its anti-anhedonia effect, arketamine might ameliorate the reduced cortical (and total) BMD seen in CSDS susceptible mice through the gut-microbiota-bone-brain axis." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36804535> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36900437_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The results demonstrated that FWG improved depression-like behaviors and increased neurotransmitter levels in the hippocampus of CUMS model rats." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36900437> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36900437_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Herein, fermented wheat germs (FWGs) were used to treat stress-induced depression." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36900437> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36931666_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "It is hoped that the results would increase the body of scientific knowledge about DSP supplementation on the cardiometabolic risk factors, oxidative stress, anti-/inflammatory biomarkers, metabolic endotoxaemia, adipokines, hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis biomarkers, immune system, anthropometric indices and mental health in patients with T2DM." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36931666> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36938477_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The potential mechanisms behind PD-related constipation include dysfunction of the enteric nervous system due to alpha-synuclein aggregation, dyssynergic contractions of the puborectalis muscle, and alterations of the gut microbiome." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36938477> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36984505_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_36984505_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "It is implicated, beyond substantiated local gastric pathologies, i.e., peptic ulcers and gastric cancer, in the pathophysiology of several neurodegenerative disorders, mainly by inducing hyperhomocysteinemia-related brain cortical thinning (BCT)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36984505> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37156128_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Our study identified distinct microbial signatures that could aid in the differentiation of DN SCZ, RISP SCZ, and HCs." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37156128> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37168424_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37168424_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The results demonstrated that the MDD group differed from the C group in terms of gut microbiota and SCFAs in the serum and that the change in certain intestinal bacteria might participate in the pathogenic mechanism of MDD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37168424> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37207228_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37207228_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Studies have shown that Toll-like receptors, especially Toll-like receptor 2 (TLR2) and Toll-like receptor 4 (TLR4), are key mediators of gut homeostasis." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37207228> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37207228_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37207228_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Notably, Toll-like receptor 2 and Toll-like receptor 4 are dysregulated in Parkinson's disease patients and may therefore be identified as the core of early gut dysfunction in Parkinson's disease." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37207228> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37212075_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37212075_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Flow cytometry was used to separate IgA-coated and -uncoated bacteria from stool samples obtained from AR and TD patients followed by amplification and sequencing of the V4 region of the 16 S rDNA gene on the MiSeq platform (Illumina)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37212075> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37228957_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The purpose of this mini-review is to provide a brief overview of the relationship between the microbiota-gut-brain axis in three neurological disorders: epilepsy, Parkinson's disease, and migraine." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37228957> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37368331_33> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37368331_33" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Phylum: Proteobacteria, its Family: <i>Enterobacteriaceae</i>, and the Genus: <i>Citrobacter</i>, <i>Klebsiella</i>, <i>Salmonella</i>, and <i>Shigella</i>; 7." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37368331> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37371676_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37371676_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Gut dysbiosis is a common factor in various AI, and diets with elevated fat and sugar content have been linked to gut microbiome alterations, contributing to increased systemic inflammation." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37371676> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37371676_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37371676_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Additionally, multiple AI's have increased levels of certain inflammatory markers such as TNF-a, IL-6, and IL-17 that have been shown to contribute to arthropathy and are also linked to increased levels of gut dysbiosis." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37371676> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37377497_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37377497_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Insights into the potential benefits of triphala polyphenols toward the promotion of resilience against stress-induced depression and cognitive impairment." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37377497> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37396336_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37396336_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Gene expression of pro-inflammatory cytokines, microglia activation-related genes, and tight junction proteins was determined in the jejunum and the hippocampus, while microbiota composition and predicted function were verified in cecum contents." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37396336> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37403161_15> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37403161_15" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Although antibiotic cocktail treatment did not change α-Syn expression in the enteric nervous system of the colon, however, reduced α-Syn expression was detected in the olfactory bulbs (forebrain) of the TG rats." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37403161> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37468912_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37468912_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "It is consistent with the BA-metabolizing genomic changes in the LDSD gut microbiota characterized by overabundances of 7-dehydroxylating bacteria and BA-inducible genes (baiCD/E/H)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37468912> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37469436_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37469436_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Compared with PS150, GR1009 have no significant hypnotic effects in the pentobarbital-induced sleep test in mice." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37469436> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37481569_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37481569_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Comparing the PD clinical phenotypes with the control group, the Mixed phenotype had significantly higher Bacteroides, Tremors predominant had lower Firmicutes and Firmicutes / Bacteroidetes ratio, and both tremors and postural instability and gait disability (PIGD) phenotypes had lower Bifidobacteria." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37481569> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37481569_13> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37481569_13" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The current study showed evidence of changes in the gut microbiome of Parkinson's disease patients compared to the healthy controls." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37481569> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37481569_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37481569_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "There was a significant increase in Bacteroides and a significant decrease of Firmicutes and Firmicutes / Bacteroidetes ratio and Bifidobacteria in PD patients." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37481569> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37485660_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37485660_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Flavonoids from Seabuckthorn (<i>Hippophae rhamnoides</i> L.) restore CUMS-induced depressive disorder and regulate the gut microbiota in mice." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37485660> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37485660_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37485660_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Seabuckthorn (<i>Hippophae rhamnoides</i> L.), which is enriched with flavonoids, including isorhamnetin, quercetin and kaempferol, is a representative example of \"medicine food homology\" targeting several diseases." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37485660> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37485660_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37485660_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In the CUMS-induced mouse model, the intake of SBF reversed their depressive behaviors and relieved the CUMS-disturbed levels of neurotrophins, neurotransmitters, stress-related hormones, and inflammation-related cytokines." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37485660> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37485660_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37485660_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Additionally, the treatment of depressive mice with SBF showed ability to regulate the gut microbiota, especially in decreasing the abundance of <i>Lactobacillaceae</i>, while increasing the abundance of <i>Lachnospiraceae</i> at the family level." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37485660> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37576972_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37576972_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Herein, we investigated the association between the metabolic status of mainland Chinese schizophrenia patients with MetS and the intestinal microbiome." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37576972> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37577447_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37577447_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The relationship between oral and gut microbiota in alcohol dependence (AD) is not well understood, particularly the effects of oral microbiota on the intestinal microbiota." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37577447> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37577447_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37577447_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Principal coordinate analysis indicated greater similarity between oral and gut microbiota in persons with AD than that in HC, and oral-gut overlaps in microbiota were found for 9 genera in persons with AD relative to only 3 genera in HC." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37577447> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37606895_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37606895_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "GI infections including that due to viral infection is known to cause postinfection disorders of gut-brain interaction (DGBI); hence, we wish to review the long-term GI consequences following COVID-19, particularly post-COVID-19 DGBI." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37606895> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37657622_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37657622_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We enrolled 57 patients with MDD and 30 healthy controls (HCs) and used 16S rRNA gene sequencing analysis and shotgun metagenomic sequencing analysis to determine gut microbial composition." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37657622> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37657622_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37657622_4" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The richness and diversity of gut microbiota in patients with MDD were the same as those in HCs, but there were differences in the abundance of Bifidobacterium and Blautia." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37657622> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37881577_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37881577_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The RSDS mice further showed significant dysregulation of gut barrier functions, including transepithelial electrical resistance, mucin homeostasis, and antimicrobial responses." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37881577> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37881577_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37881577_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Behavioral studies, metagenomics analysis of the microbiome, gut permeability assay (on mouse colon, using an Ussing chamber), immunoblotting, and immunohistochemical analyses were performed." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37881577> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37900921_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37900921_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We conclude that future research should focus on physical (e.g., ingestion of sorbents) or metabolic mechanisms (e.g., conversion to 4EP-glucuronide) that are capable of being used as interventions to reduce the flux of 4EP from the gut into the body, increase the efflux of 4EP and/or 4EPS from the brain, or increase excretion from the kidneys as a means of addressing the neurological impacts of 4EP." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37900921> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37900921_5> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37900921_5" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We note that increased intestinal permeability is common in autistic individuals, potentially explaining increased flux of 4EP and/or 4EPS across the gut epithelium and the Blood Brain Barrier [BBB]." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37900921> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37927130_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37927130_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Mental health is influenced by the gut-brain axis; for example, gut dysbiosis has been observed in patients with major depressive disorder (MDD)." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37927130> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37927130_10> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37927130_10" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We further demonstrated the role of <i>Htr1a</i> using AAV-shRNA to downregulate <i>Htr1a</i> in the mPFC of CUS mice, effectively reversing CUS-induced anhedonic behavior." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37927130> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37927130_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37927130_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "F4 consumption reduced the elevated levels of serotonin (5-HT) in the brain observed in the CUS group." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37927130> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37960197_7> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37960197_7" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The analysis of the 196 gut microbiota revealed that <i>genus</i>_<i>Ruminococcaceae</i> (<i>UCG009</i>) (P<sub>IVW</sub> = 0.010) and <i>genus</i>_<i>Subdoligranulum</i> (P<sub>IVW</sub> = 0.041) were associated with an increased risk of OSA onset." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37960197> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37960197_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37960197_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Conversely, <i>Family</i>_<i>Ruminococcaceae</i> (P<sub>IVW</sub> = 0.030), <i>genus</i>_<i>Coprococcus2</i> (P<sub>WM</sub> = 0.025), <i>genus</i>_<i>Eggerthella</i> (P<sub>IVW</sub> = 0.011), and <i>genus</i>_<i>Eubacterium</i> (<i>xylanophilum</i>_<i>group</i>) (P<sub>IVW</sub> = 0.001) were negatively related to the risk of OSA." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37960197> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37995075_11> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_37995075_11" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Gut microbe-related DEGs of CREB3L3 and CCDC173 were possible molecular biomarkers and therapeutic targets of women with PCOS-DP." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37995075> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/38010793_8> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_38010793_8" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "More importantly, three increased microbiota including <i>Turicibacter</i>, <i>Coprococcus 1</i>, and Eggerthellaceae positively modulated the associations of unbalanced dietary intake with constipation and total GI symptoms, and the decreased <i>Clostridium sp. BR31</i>" ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/38010793> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/38011787_0> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_38011787_0" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Cryptotanshinone regulates gut microbiota and PI3K-AKT pathway in rats to alleviate CUMS induced depressive symptoms." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/38011787> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/38068763_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_38068763_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The consumption of vegetables and whole grain cereals increased (DQI-I adequacy), the consumption of simple sugars and SFA decreased (moderation DQI-I), and the consumption of monounsaturated fatty acids increased it." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/38068763> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/38204948_9> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_38204948_9" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Studies show that dietary factors such as probiotics and micronutrient supplementation may significantly improve psychiatric symptoms in PCOS patients while helping regulate neurotransmitter levels in the body." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/38204948> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/38229613_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_38229613_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "We sequenced microbial DNA using fecal samples collected from PD cases and healthy controls (HCs) to evaluate the role of gut microbiota." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/38229613> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/38229613_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_38229613_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Genus <i>Akkermansia</i>, <i>Dialister</i>, <i>Bacteroides</i>, and <i>Lachnospiraceae NK4A136</i> group positively correlated with constipation in PD." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/38229613> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/38247868_1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_38247868_1" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Inflammatory bowel disease (IBD), a common term for Crohn's disease and ulcerative colitis, is a chronic, relapse-remitting condition of the gastrointestinal tract that is increasing worldwide." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/38247868> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/38247868_2> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_38247868_2" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Psychiatric comorbidities, including depression and anxiety, are more prevalent in IBD patients than in healthy individuals." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/38247868> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/38260914_3> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_38260914_3" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "The gut-skin axis explains a bidirectional interaction between skin and gut microbiota in some inflammatory skin diseases such as atopic dermatitis, psoriasis, or rosacea." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/38260914> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/38278499_6> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_38278499_6" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "In the GP cohort, consumption of six or more doses per week was associated with low hippuric acid concentrations, similar to those observed in the MDD cohort, but in these individuals it was regardless of their level of alcohol use." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/38278499> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/38302874_13> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_38302874_13" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "qPCR results revealed modifications in the expression of serotonin-related intestinal genes in PIPO patients, when compared to controls." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/38302874> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/38302874_15> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_38302874_15" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "For the first time, we report in PIPO patients a specific MAM associated to underlying pathology and an altered intestinal serotonin pathway." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/38302874> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/38409102_16> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_38409102_16" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "Alterations in the microbial short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs), were also observed, with major and minor SCFAs being lower in SPS-susceptible males whereas branched-chain SCFAs being higher in SPS-susceptible females." ;
    gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/38409102> .

<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/38409102_22> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        gutprop:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence_38409102_22" ;
    gutprop:hasSentenceText "SPS-resilient males displayed elevated cecal acetate levels, whereas SPS-susceptible females exhibited heightened branched-chain SCFAs." ;
